<node id="Control Engineering">
  <data key="d0">Control Engineering</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Control Engineering is a field focused on designing systems to behave in a desired manner, often through the use of linearized models.&lt;SEP&gt;Control engineering is a field focused on designing systems that manage and regulate other systems using feedback and control actions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c4592f010cac7379fc36d89be453d068&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b1e646fef80acb88f1ef990e507e7d48</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Physical Systems">
  <data key="d0">Physical Systems</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Physical systems refer to tangible systems that can be represented by block diagrams to analyze their dynamic behavior.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c4592f010cac7379fc36d89be453d068</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
