  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">An electronic circuit symbol represents operations or processes in electrical engineering, often used in diagrams.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c4592f010cac7379fc36d89be453d068</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Summing Point">
  <data key="d0">Summing Point</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">A summing point in a control system diagram is where multiple input signals are algebraically summed.&lt;SEP&gt;A summing point is a component in a block diagram that combines multiple input signals to produce a control signal.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e8171fcc2a296f92a6bcda8de5f8a214&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8b50aac79f087fdc5dd68834ab09cb3</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Block G(s)">
  <data key="d0">Block G(s)</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Block G(s) represents a transfer function or mathematical model of a physical component in a control system, such as an amplifier or filter.&lt;SEP&gt;Block G(s) represents another transfer function or system component that processes the signal received from Block G_c(s) in a control system.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e8171fcc2a296f92a6bcda8de5f8a214&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab1222a4f68b9900993c6bdde861432b</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Block C(s)">
  <data key="d0">Block C(s)</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Block C(s) is another transfer function or mathematical model within the control system, processing control signals to produce response signals.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e8171fcc2a296f92a6bcda8de5f8a214</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Block Diagram of a Closed-Loop System">
  <data key="d0">Block Diagram of a Closed-Loop System</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">A block diagram of a closed-loop system is a schematic representation used to model and analyze complex control systems with feedback loops.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e8171fcc2a296f92a6bcda8de5f8a214</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Feedback Element">
  <data key="d0">Feedback Element</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The feedback element in a control system modifies the output signal before it is compared with the input, often implemented as a sensor.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e8171fcc2a296f92a6bcda8de5f8a214</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Input Signal (R(s))">
  <data key="d0">Input Signal (R(s))</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">R(s) is the input signal to the control system, representing the desired reference value.&lt;SEP&gt;The input signal R(s) is the initial signal or command that enters the control system to be processed.&lt;SEP&gt;The reference or desired output of the control system, represented by a circle with an arrow in the block diagram.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e8171fcc2a296f92a6bcda8de5f8a214&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03cc52015d502a70a9646315437485f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a599688f3c870bb8d72b6239047bad9</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Controller (E(s))">
  <data key="d0">Controller (E(s))</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The controller processes the input signal to generate an error signal E(s), regulating the system's behavior.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e8171fcc2a296f92a6bcda8de5f8a214</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Process (G(s))">
  <data key="d0">Process (G(s))</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The process, represented by G(s), transforms the output of the controller into a new signal to achieve the desired outcome.</data>
