<node id="Transfer Matrix">
  <data key="d0">Transfer Matrix</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The Transfer Matrix is a mathematical representation used in control systems to describe the input-output relationship in multi-input, multi-output systems. It combines Equations (2–56) and (2–57) to effectively represent the system's transfer functions. This matrix representation extends the concept of transfer functions by providing a comprehensive view of the system dynamics, relating input and output signals through matrix notation. It is particularly useful for analyzing the dynamics of systems with multiple inputs and outputs, where it relates the output vector to the input vector, offering a detailed depiction of the system's behavior.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0477d9985a7d5b2045fb80504b1c802a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-817b95a5144d0dce10f2c3a02063acbe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76155cfacd298ba99866d06587bc0e7d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a7e6ee6eefc1562c87e6317d173028b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c002c8164af0baaf62d1b67662dbbda4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b0975c8819fd43e77406652cac9bd23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30afd1ea0d3bf0f6ff1f6ab5550759e8</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
