<node id="Canonical Form">
  <data key="d0">Canonical Form</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Canonical forms are specific types of state-space representations, including controllable, observable, diagonal, and Jordan forms, used for simplifying system analysis.&lt;SEP&gt;The controllable canonical form is a standardized representation of the state equation that facilitates control design.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0e2680709d2b529eb353b1601aca0714&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c59263c3980c23b4b65459cfd0557ec</data>
