</node>
<node id="Nonlinear Systems">
  <data key="d0">Nonlinear Systems</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Nonlinear Systems are systems where the principle of superposition does not apply, and the response to inputs cannot be calculated by treating one input at a time.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b1e646fef80acb88f1ef990e507e7d48</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Taylor Series Expansion">
  <data key="d0">Taylor Series Expansion</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Taylor Series Expansion is a mathematical method for approximating functions using series expansion.&lt;SEP&gt;Taylor Series Expansion is a mathematical method used to approximate nonlinear functions by expanding them around an operating point and retaining linear terms.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b1e646fef80acb88f1ef990e507e7d48&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76155cfacd298ba99866d06587bc0e7d</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Linearization">
  <data key="d0">Linearization</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Linearization is the process of approximating a nonlinear system by a linear system around an equilibrium point.&lt;SEP&gt;Linearization refers to the process of approximating a nonlinear equation by a linear one near a specific operating point.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4178d8ac5083f4ba940096cd490ec0cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b1e646fef80acb88f1ef990e507e7d48</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Equilibrium Point">
  <data key="d0">Equilibrium Point</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">An Equilibrium Point is a state around which a system operates, allowing for linearization in control engineering.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b1e646fef80acb88f1ef990e507e7d48</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Taylor Series">
  <data key="d0">Taylor Series</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">A mathematical series used to approximate functions around a specific point by expanding them into polynomials.&lt;SEP&gt;Taylor Series is a mathematical tool used to approximate functions by expanding them into a series of terms based on derivatives.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-80d07add21c293cc285a7efb53eea548&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-adb718308239fee157c153fdd63d6ea6</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Nonlinear System">
  <data key="d0">Nonlinear System</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">A nonlinear system is one where the output is not directly proportional to the input, often requiring complex models for analysis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-80d07add21c293cc285a7efb53eea548</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Linear Approximation">
  <data key="d0">Linear Approximation</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Linear Approximation involves approximating a nonlinear function by a linear function, often used in mathematical modeling.&lt;SEP&gt;Linear approximation refers to the process of simplifying a nonlinear system by approximating it with linear equations near a specific operating point.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-80d07add21c293cc285a7efb53eea548&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a34c150b7357f195267cedd77a6ab328</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Operating Point">
  <data key="d0">Operating Point</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">An operating point is a set of conditions (values of variables) under which a system operates, used as a reference for linearization.&lt;SEP&gt;The normal operating point is where the system variables are zero, providing a baseline for analysis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9ec9bff7736610bd695d1b222222e6f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-80d07add21c293cc285a7efb53eea548</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Partial Derivatives">
  <data key="d0">Partial Derivatives</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Partial derivatives are derivatives of functions with multiple variables, indicating how the function changes with respect to one variable, holding others constant.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-80d07add21c293cc285a7efb53eea548</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Error Calculation">
  <data key="d0">Error Calculation</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Error calculation involves determining the difference between the actual value and the estimated value provided by a model or approximation.&lt;SEP&gt;The difference between the exact value and the linearized equation value, calculated as 1 or 2%.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-80d07add21c293cc285a7efb53eea548&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-adb718308239fee157c153fdd63d6ea6</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
