<node id="CO2 Conversion Process">
  <data key="d0">CO2 Conversion Process</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The process involves converting carbon dioxide (CO2) into oxygen (O2) through stages of water splitting, hydrogen atom transfer, and oxygen molecule formation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d0ef5febc821439635564c2c2af2c325</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Water Splitting">
  <data key="d0">Water Splitting</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Water splitting is a stage in the CO2 conversion process where water molecules are split into hydrogen atoms and oxygen ions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d0ef5febc821439635564c2c2af2c325</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Electrolysis">
  <data key="d0">Electrolysis</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Electrolysis is a process represented in the CO2 conversion diagram, involving the flow of electrons between electrodes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d0ef5febc821439635564c2c2af2c325</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Oxygen Molecule Formation">
  <data key="d0">Oxygen Molecule Formation</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Oxygen molecule formation is the final stage in converting CO2 into O2, where oxygen ions combine to form oxygen molecules.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d0ef5febc821439635564c2c2af2c325</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
