  <data key="d0">G1-G4</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">G1-G4 are components within the block diagram that process signals in sequence, indicating a linear flow of information.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d0ef5febc821439635564c2c2af2c325</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="H1-H3">
  <data key="d0">H1-H3</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">H1-H3 are components in the block diagram that may represent additional processing steps or branches.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d0ef5febc821439635564c2c2af2c325</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Gf">
  <data key="d0">Gf</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">A block that likely represents a filter or gain adjustment in the control system.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3c0ec79f7d7ca60c30e8465fa9c98468</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Gc">
  <data key="d0">Gc</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">A block that likely represents a filter or gain adjustment in the control system.&lt;SEP&gt;Gc is a label used to identify a specific component or output within the diagram.&lt;SEP&gt;Gc represents the compensator in the system, with specific magnitude and phase responses.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b987c9f4905e5b5d570e0dc620016e58&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d685d32ace4fbb1daf3dfa98d88fd29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c0ec79f7d7ca60c30e8465fa9c98468</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="H">
  <data key="d0">H</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">A block that might signify a transformation or processing step within the control system.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3c0ec79f7d7ca60c30e8465fa9c98468</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="E(s)">
  <data key="d0">E(s)</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">E(s) is a crucial component in control systems, serving as an error signal that represents the difference between the desired output and the actual output. It functions as part of the system's control loop and is involved in determining the transfer function C(s)/E(s). E(s) acts as an error detector or feedback mechanism, comparing expected outputs with actual ones to generate error signals internally. Additionally, E(s) can be seen as the input signal being transformed within the system, highlighting its role in influencing the system's overall performance and stability.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-45a3caf311e2ab85a8b8795fbe5c9365&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da45ed46b3417493dc6e2a6d545bd8ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c0ec79f7d7ca60c30e8465fa9c98468&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3dac0ceabd7b52fc29d821c18da7fcb1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd104ba0a5d1c1ab6f6f3b08f2715be8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e67cb8477adc7c0ef97482e4e7be7fa4</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="U(s)">
  <data key="d0">U(s)</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">A block that could denote control inputs to the plant being controlled.&lt;SEP&gt;U(s) is an actuator block in control systems that processes the output of Gc(s).&lt;SEP&gt;U(s) is another intermediate signal, originating from R(s), used in further signal processing stages.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3c0ec79f7d7ca60c30e8465fa9c98468&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e67cb8477adc7c0ef97482e4e7be7fa4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-799625a96afba94ba9a1c4461a64170d</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="D(s)">
  <data key="d0">D(s)</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">D(s) is a component within an electrical circuit, represented in a technical diagram. It serves various roles in the system, acting as both a filter component in the signal processing system and a block that might represent compensators or controllers adjusting system behavior based on feedback. D(s) is the output from a block that takes inputs from Gc1(s) and Gc2(s), contributing to the signal processing flow. It is also associated with the disturbance input signal in control systems, which can affect the system's performance and stability. Additionally, D(s) is connected to a gain block labeled G3, and an input signal is added to the processed output from C2(s). Overall, D(s) plays a multifaceted role in the system, contributing to both input and output processes and influencing system stability and behavior.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-273f66b6e44351603fc5160de59ad839&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-799625a96afba94ba9a1c4461a64170d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8b50aac79f087fdc5dd68834ab09cb3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d4db33b4e6388556833f75db47703f2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b987c9f4905e5b5d570e0dc620016e58&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c0ec79f7d7ca60c30e8465fa9c98468&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-952ac88fc20d94741d460ff36bcefd2c</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
