<node id="State-Space Model">
  <data key="d0">State-Space Model</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">A mathematical model describing the system dynamics of the LC circuit using state variables.&lt;SEP&gt;A state-space model is a representation of the system in standard form, involving matrices that define the dynamics and outputs of the system.&lt;SEP&gt;State-Space Model is a mathematical representation of the system's dynamics using state variables.&lt;SEP&gt;The state-space model is a mathematical representation of a physical system in terms of its state variables and is used for designing and analyzing control systems.&lt;SEP&gt;The state-space model is a mathematical representation of a physical system using state variables and equations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-45d58fa0ad7e2ced2585b4512c2f59e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32e837730a9d05b1df592f0ae66e9fc2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dfd846455e2fefcbadf8b8c8b3d71195&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-925099acac18f050f91f2ea8c404ad69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-683d619a6a6debc5b41f0a5860aa0746</data>
