  <data key="d3">chunk-0f3c134e307adcb9587e648683f4f4b0</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="MATLAB Program">
  <data key="d0">MATLAB Program</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The MATLAB Program is a versatile software environment and high-level programming language used for numerical computation, data analysis, and visualization. It is particularly prominent in engineering and scientific fields for tasks such as plotting and analyzing control systems. The program is designed to simulate responses of systems, such as the inverted pendulum system, and can generate plots like the root locus plot to showcase the relationship between the input and output of control systems. Additionally, MATLAB is employed to produce transfer functions and compute optimal values of parameters for control systems, such as K and a. It is also used to solve optimization problems by applying filters to input signals with coefficients calculated from arrays. Furthermore, the program calculates observer gain and transfer functions for observer controllers in systems with multiple states, inputs, and outputs. Overall, MATLAB is a comprehensive platform for analyzing and designing systems, as well as generating various system response plots.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-577f4c0582663d9533ba9e75104e8038&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4178d8ac5083f4ba940096cd490ec0cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c0dd560e406cc5769efa44c166402303&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e943fefbd15dc3bfc97bcb9515cd1eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d4db33b4e6388556833f75db47703f2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-681185e57d810ae79c2ee826ac8ba784&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c39c97551687b0bf865de0bebf31277&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2db63f41e22678b776f42091570392a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ceb4d77b2cbe8e502eaa62894b68c016&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8bb8d79a4bce9c3a0571e1ec2592d1a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c3a55af272f2092fd9d053a8d89af4b4</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
