<node id="Error Signal">
  <data key="d0">Error Signal</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">A signal indicating the difference between a desired setpoint and the actual value, used to adjust the system.&lt;SEP&gt;Error Signal is the difference between the input and output of a system, indicating deviation from desired performance.&lt;SEP&gt;The Error Signal is calculated as the difference between the reference input and the current output in a control system.&lt;SEP&gt;The Error Signal is the difference between the desired output and the actual output of the plant, used to adjust the controller's output.&lt;SEP&gt;The resulting signal from the comparison between the input and output, used to adjust the system's performance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7cb24308be90f4de9c5775f0a3a25ce9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-219f7fb5973694e4ed3fc49b9c5d4c60&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c123c891021bce024d99af35fd34585&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-feef65cbaf78b28598f6c9d649127cbd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5743b50920c06e8fe8331392a198cbcc</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
