</node>
<node id="Newton's Second Law">
  <data key="d0">Newton's Second Law</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Newton's Second Law is a fundamental principle governing mechanical systems, stating that the force acting on an object is equal to the mass of the object times its acceleration.&lt;SEP&gt;Newton's Second Law is a fundamental principle of physics applied in the derivation of equations for the suspension system.&lt;SEP&gt;Newton's Second Law is a fundamental principle of physics used to describe the motion of the cart.&lt;SEP&gt;Newton's Second Law of motion, F = ma, is applied to the system to model the forces and acceleration.&lt;SEP&gt;Newton's second law of motion states that the acceleration of an object is directly proportional to the net force acting on it and inversely proportional to its mass.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-48f6fb89274b6880175da471dd77be24&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f800baebc1ea569d8d6199edc2fa8f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-201ad2bff594c69ddcdebbbde0310588&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-683d619a6a6debc5b41f0a5860aa0746&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a99de50670eed69da300e8009547bd36</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
