  <data key="d0">Springs in Series</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Springs in series are a configuration where multiple springs are connected end to end, affecting the equivalent spring constant.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a99de50670eed69da300e8009547bd36</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Equivalent Spring Constant">
  <data key="d0">Equivalent Spring Constant</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The equivalent spring constant is a measure of the combined stiffness of springs in a mechanical system, calculated differently for parallel and series configurations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a99de50670eed69da300e8009547bd36</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="External Force F">
  <data key="d0">External Force F</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">External Force F is a force acting on a mechanical system, causing displacement or motion of the mass and affecting the springs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a99de50670eed69da300e8009547bd36</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="State-Space Models">
  <data key="d0">State-Space Models</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">State-space models represent systems using state variables and equations to describe their dynamics.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a99de50670eed69da300e8009547bd36</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Dashpot">
  <data key="d0">Dashpot</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">A dashpot is a mechanical device primarily used to dampen motion through viscous friction. It consists of a piston and an oil-filled cylinder, which absorbs energy and dissipates it as heat without storing kinetic or potential energy. Dashpots are integral components within hydraulic systems, where they play a crucial role in damping and controlling fluid movement. Often referred to as dampers, they act as differentiating elements in system models, affecting the displacement of a piston and resisting motion. Dashpots are commonly found in various mechanical systems to provide effective damping and control.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f104d09d0c472d244729f4c0273b66e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4af75b278219735803bd2d9c41d781d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f9976290aaf5bc6b5c7806f43bcf303&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da45ed46b3417493dc6e2a6d545bd8ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-62a1cbf10c33f82d65ca8e2a6d86b67b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-faf6d229bd33d9a677ddb2c4f3fe8552</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Equivalent Spring Constant (k_eq)">
  <data key="d0">Equivalent Spring Constant (k_eq)</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The equivalent spring constant, denoted as k_eq, is a measure used to describe the combined stiffness of two or more springs in a system.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4af75b278219735803bd2d9c41d781d9</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Equivalent Viscous-Friction Coefficient (b_eq)">
  <data key="d0">Equivalent Viscous-Friction Coefficient (b_eq)</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The equivalent viscous-friction coefficient, denoted as b_eq, is a measure used to describe the combined damping effect of two or more dampers in a system.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4af75b278219735803bd2d9c41d781d9</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Force (F)">
  <data key="d0">Force (F)</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Force is a physical quantity that represents the interaction between objects, often resulting in a change in motion. In this context, it is related to the spring and damper systems.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4af75b278219735803bd2d9c41d781d9</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
