<node id="Springs and Masses System">
  <data key="d0">Springs and Masses System</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Springs and Masses System is depicted in the image, consisting of blocks 'm1' and 'm2' connected by springs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-683d619a6a6debc5b41f0a5860aa0746</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Mass m1">
  <data key="d0">Mass m1</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">A mass in the mechanical system, subject to forces from the spring and regulator.&lt;SEP&gt;Mass m1 is one of the two masses in the Suspension System, connected to a spring and influenced by external forces.&lt;SEP&gt;Mass m1 is the first mass in the mechanical system, subjected to an external force.&lt;SEP&gt;Mass m1 is the left block in the mechanical system, influenced by springs and external force.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-23de25452ffebaa5122b237d5ec13605&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd87696d65a75079f4edb623b979b62f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b5c28d651a853ceed5a2bb812c9fd2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7b84f68967e01f789185103a6da424fa</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Mass m2">
  <data key="d0">Mass m2</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Another mass in the mechanical system, interacting with Mass m1 through the spring.&lt;SEP&gt;Mass m2 is the right block in the mechanical system, connected to m1 by springs.&lt;SEP&gt;Mass m2 is the second mass in the Suspension System, also connected to a spring and influenced by external forces.&lt;SEP&gt;Mass m2 is the second mass in the mechanical system, connected by springs and dampers.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-23de25452ffebaa5122b237d5ec13605&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd87696d65a75079f4edb623b979b62f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b5c28d651a853ceed5a2bb812c9fd2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7b84f68967e01f789185103a6da424fa</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Springs">
  <data key="d0">Springs</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Springs are components of the mechanical system, connecting masses and the wall, with one spring not clearly connected.&lt;SEP&gt;Springs are components of the suspension system represented by coiled springs that connect the car's frame to its wheels.&lt;SEP&gt;Springs are mechanical components represented by coiled lines with arrows, used to illustrate force and motion.&lt;SEP&gt;Springs are mechanical components that connect masses in the system, exerting forces proportional to their compression or stretching.&lt;SEP&gt;Springs connect the masses in the mechanical system, depicted as wavy lines with stiffness constants k1 and k3.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-48f6fb89274b6880175da471dd77be24&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-23de25452ffebaa5122b237d5ec13605&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd87696d65a75079f4edb623b979b62f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b5c28d651a853ceed5a2bb812c9fd2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da4cffe0215472e30c589d1be7e6d819</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="External Force u">
  <data key="d0">External Force u</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">External Force u is an arrow indicating a force acting on the mechanical system.&lt;SEP&gt;External Force u is applied to the first mass m1 in the mechanical system.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-23de25452ffebaa5122b237d5ec13605&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd87696d65a75079f4edb623b979b62f</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Equation of Motion">
  <data key="d0">Equation of Motion</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The Equation of Motion describes the dynamic behavior of the mechanical system, incorporating mass, damping, and stiffness elements.&lt;SEP&gt;The equation of motion describes the dynamics of the harmonic oscillator system using Newton's second law, involving mass, damping, and spring constant.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fd87696d65a75079f4edb623b979b62f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-284988f822bbc861f6935dafb7bde2c7</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Inverted Pendulum System">
  <data key="d0">Inverted Pendulum System</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">A mechanical system consisting of a mass, spring, and pendulum, analyzed for dynamics and control.&lt;SEP&gt;Inverted Pendulum System is a mechanical system with a mass evenly distributed along the length of the rod.&lt;SEP&gt;The inverted pendulum system is a control system designed to maintain the pendulum in a vertical position despite disturbances.&lt;SEP&gt;The inverted pendulum system is a model used for attitude control of a space booster during takeoff, requiring control forces to maintain vertical stability.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a7d35d4c0a78082736add717b2833c58&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-23de25452ffebaa5122b237d5ec13605&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c0dd560e406cc5769efa44c166402303&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7bd9d9a9ccff6dcc7aa39644785f5940</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Motor-driven Cart">
  <data key="d0">Motor-driven Cart</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The motor-driven cart is a component of the inverted pendulum system, used to apply control forces to maintain stability.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a7d35d4c0a78082736add717b2833c58</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Space Booster">
  <data key="d0">Space Booster</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The space booster is a vehicle that requires attitude control to remain vertical during takeoff, modeled by the inverted pendulum system.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a7d35d4c0a78082736add717b2833c58</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
