<node id="Resistors">
  <data key="d0">Resistors</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Resistors (R1-R4) are components in the circuit diagrams that influence the gain and signal processing within the PID controller.&lt;SEP&gt;Resistors are components in the circuit diagrams that provide resistance to the flow of electric current.&lt;SEP&gt;Resistors are components in the electric circuit diagram, labeled as R1, R2, R3, and R4, used for controlling current flow.&lt;SEP&gt;Resistors are components used in electronic circuits to regulate current flow and divide voltages, often used in conjunction with op-amps.&lt;SEP&gt;Resistors are electrical components that provide resistance in the circuit, denoted as R1, R2, R3.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-491a839e54fff3c9e325de4c696089cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8575f9998ffcb80f46b6bfa2a8177e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fae6e2215ca8025e75a73079e64a6fbc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c9880f98c8d7623b2a11ce706897bd2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e178c5a5d1b6a385f1612387424d850a</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Capacitors">
  <data key="d0">Capacitors</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Capacitors (C1-C2) are components in the circuit diagrams that affect the signal processing and frequency response in the PID controller.&lt;SEP&gt;Capacitors are components in the circuit diagrams that store electrical energy temporarily.&lt;SEP&gt;Capacitors are electrical components that store energy, denoted as C1 and C2.&lt;SEP&gt;Capacitors in the circuit, labeled as C1 and C2, are components used for storing electrical energy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-491a839e54fff3c9e325de4c696089cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fae6e2215ca8025e75a73079e64a6fbc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8575f9998ffcb80f46b6bfa2a8177e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e178c5a5d1b6a385f1612387424d850a</data>
