  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">A versatile electronic component used to amplify voltage signals, often found in circuits for signal processing and control applications.&lt;SEP&gt;An operational amplifier is a key component in electronic circuits, used here as an integrator.&lt;SEP&gt;An operational amplifier is a key component in the circuit, represented by a triangle symbol, used for signal processing and amplification.&lt;SEP&gt;An operational amplifier is a versatile electronic device used in various configurations, such as inverting, noninverting, differential, and integrator circuits, to amplify voltage signals.&lt;SEP&gt;The operational amplifier is a crucial component in the circuit, used for amplifying signals.</data>
