<node id="Differential Amplifier">
  <data key="d0">Differential Amplifier</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">A differential amplifier is a circuit configuration using an op-amp to amplify the difference between two input signals, often used in audio equipment.&lt;SEP&gt;A differential amplifier is a type of amplifier that amplifies the difference between two input voltages, using operational amplifiers with high differential gain.&lt;SEP&gt;A differential amplifier is a type of operational-amplifier configuration that amplifies the voltage difference between two input signals.&lt;SEP&gt;Differential Amplifier is a device that amplifies the difference between two input signals.</data>
