<node id="Negative Feedback">
  <data key="d0">Negative Feedback</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Negative feedback in an amplifier is a mechanism where a portion of the output is fed back to the input to stabilize and control the gain of the amplifier.&lt;SEP&gt;Negative feedback is a control system mechanism that helps stabilize the system by reducing the difference between desired and actual output.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8230d3f2f6d179c68a787d4d88412e94&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c9880f98c8d7623b2a11ce706897bd2</data>
