  <data key="d2">A resistor used in the operational amplifier circuit, contributing to the input impedance and affecting the transfer function.&lt;SEP&gt;Resistor R1 is a component in the electrical circuit, opposing the flow of current.&lt;SEP&gt;Resistor R1 is an electrical component with a resistance of 10 Ω, part of a series circuit in Figure 3–30.&lt;SEP&gt;Resistor R1 is an electrical component with a resistance value of 1000 Ohms, used in various circuit configurations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-080439bdd387ba07fa0b308cc5ef8916&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5df7e896b70c3eb7634619fc0cc39c79&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d61c2c5328f39dc98d3d82a63c5fe2b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-23de25452ffebaa5122b237d5ec13605</data>
