<node id="Resistor R2">
  <data key="d0">Resistor R2</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">A resistor used in the operational amplifier circuit, contributing to the feedback impedance and affecting the transfer function.&lt;SEP&gt;Resistor R2 is a component in the op-amp circuit, forming part of the voltage divider with the capacitor.&lt;SEP&gt;Resistor R2 is an electrical component with a resistance of 20 Ω, part of a series circuit in Figure 3–30.&lt;SEP&gt;Resistor R2 is an electrical component, part of the op-amp circuit, connected between the inverting input and ground.&lt;SEP&gt;Resistor R2 is another component in the electrical circuit, opposing the flow of current.</data>
