  <data key="d0">Masses</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Masses refer to the components of the spring-mass system, specifically m1 and m2, which are connected by springs and subject to external forces.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3b5c28d651a853ceed5a2bb812c9fd2d</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Dashpots">
  <data key="d0">Dashpots</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Dashpots are viscous damping components attached to the blocks in the mechanical system, opposing motion and providing damping forces.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3b5c28d651a853ceed5a2bb812c9fd2d</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="External Forces">
  <data key="d0">External Forces</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">External Forces are forces applied to the blocks in the system, causing motion and acceleration relative to each other.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3b5c28d651a853ceed5a2bb812c9fd2d</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Equilibrium">
  <data key="d0">Equilibrium</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Equilibrium is a state indicated by equal forces on either side of a fulcrum, representing balance within a system.&lt;SEP&gt;Equilibrium refers to the state where forces acting on the masses balance each other, resulting in no motion.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-da4cffe0215472e30c589d1be7e6d819&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b5c28d651a853ceed5a2bb812c9fd2d</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Oscillation">
  <data key="d0">Oscillation</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Oscillation is the motion of the system when displaced from equilibrium, driven by restoring forces exerted by the springs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3b5c28d651a853ceed5a2bb812c9fd2d</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
