<node id="Servo System">
  <data key="d0">Servo System</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">A control system featuring a servomotor, potentiometers, amplifier, and other components to measure and correct angular position errors.&lt;SEP&gt;A control system that uses feedback to control the position or speed of a motor.&lt;SEP&gt;A mechanical system designed to use feedback to control and maintain a desired output, often involving position and velocity signals.&lt;SEP&gt;A servo system is a second-order control system that includes a proportional controller and load elements for controlling output position in response to input.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d8575f9998ffcb80f46b6bfa2a8177e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e045a2c6fa20bf1beb094683eabf565&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-caf32671a4ee19f2726367a3b3826926&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-421dc885fedffcbdd1023734df76f5f1</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Servomotor">
  <data key="d0">Servomotor</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">A DC motor in the servo system designed for use in control systems to develop torque and correct position errors.&lt;SEP&gt;A servomotor is a device that uses fluid pressure to control the movement of a mechanical load, featuring components like the pump, motor, valve, and load.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fdb46bdfea03c8ad1daae623cf71c4a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8575f9998ffcb80f46b6bfa2a8177e8</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Potentiometers">
  <data key="d0">Potentiometers</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Potentiometers in the servo system act as error-measuring devices, converting positions into proportional electric signals.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d8575f9998ffcb80f46b6bfa2a8177e8</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Torque">
  <data key="d0">Torque</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Torque developed by the servomotor to reduce angular position error to zero, proportional to armature current.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d8575f9998ffcb80f46b6bfa2a8177e8</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Back EMF">
  <data key="d0">Back EMF</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Back EMF refers to the electromotive force that opposes the current in the motor, effectively increasing the viscous friction in the system.&lt;SEP&gt;Back electromotive force in the servomotor, proportional to angular velocity and induced in the armature.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d8575f9998ffcb80f46b6bfa2a8177e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d61c2c5328f39dc98d3d82a63c5fe2b</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Control Theory">
  <data key="d0">Control Theory</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Control Theory is a field of study focused on the behavior of dynamical systems with inputs, particularly in engineering.&lt;SEP&gt;Control theory is a field of study that deals with the behavior of dynamical systems with inputs and how to modify the output by changes in the input.&lt;SEP&gt;Control theory is an interdisciplinary branch of engineering and mathematics focused on the behavior of dynamical systems with inputs.&lt;SEP&gt;Theoretical framework related to the system diagram, involving signal processing and control of dynamic systems.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d8575f9998ffcb80f46b6bfa2a8177e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab41d39cf3a8cfab5c7e12464cab8a94&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76bc75a542f1bbffc63059af2a43bbeb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54fdf618f95ac183086f742904f0c8d6</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Error Voltage">
  <data key="d0">Error Voltage</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The voltage difference between input and output positions in the servo system, used to drive the motor.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d8575f9998ffcb80f46b6bfa2a8177e8</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Gear Train">
  <data key="d0">Gear Train</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">A gear train is a mechanical system composed of multiple gears and levers, used to illustrate mechanical operations and concepts.&lt;SEP&gt;A mechanical system in the servo system that transmits motion from the motor to the output shaft, altering speed and torque.&lt;SEP&gt;The gear train transmits rotational motion from the motor, altering speed and torque.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fdb46bdfea03c8ad1daae623cf71c4a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8575f9998ffcb80f46b6bfa2a8177e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-421dc885fedffcbdd1023734df76f5f1</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Load">
  <data key="d0">Load</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The load is the end component of the system, receiving torque from Shaft 4.&lt;SEP&gt;The load is the mechanical component controlled by the servomotor, which can be a linear actuator, rotary actuator, or other mechanical device.&lt;SEP&gt;The load is the mechanical component controlled by the servomotor, which can be adjusted in real-time.&lt;SEP&gt;The load receives controlled output and provides feedback to the controller in a system.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fdb46bdfea03c8ad1daae623cf71c4a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f63499af2a9ae0d75cf56aad0cf76999&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-344b982779dae543f1e2fa4c92c88748&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-421dc885fedffcbdd1023734df76f5f1</data>
