<node id="Motor">
  <data key="d0">Motor</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">A component positioned below the valve in the mechanical system diagram, represented by the label 'M', indicating downward motion.&lt;SEP&gt;A motor in a hydraulic servomotor converts high-pressure fluid into rotational motion.&lt;SEP&gt;The motor converts amplified signals into rotational motion in a control system.&lt;SEP&gt;The motor converts high-pressure fluid into rotational motion, controlling the load.&lt;SEP&gt;The motor provides the initial input torque, $T_m(t)$, to the mechanical system.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f63499af2a9ae0d75cf56aad0cf76999&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-344b982779dae543f1e2fa4c92c88748&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-421dc885fedffcbdd1023734df76f5f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db868c08afc68de9d8850f06c963dfd1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fdb46bdfea03c8ad1daae623cf71c4a1</data>
