  <data key="d0">Spring-Loaded Pendulum System</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">A mechanical system consisting of a pendulum and a spring, where the spring force is zero when the pendulum is vertical.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-201ad2bff594c69ddcdebbbde0310588</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Simple Harmonic Oscillator">
  <data key="d0">Simple Harmonic Oscillator</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">A Simple Harmonic Oscillator is a system that exhibits periodic motion, often used in physics and engineering.&lt;SEP&gt;A basic physics model consisting of a mass connected to a spring, used to describe oscillatory motion.&lt;SEP&gt;A fundamental concept in physics, depicted by a mass suspended from a spring, exhibiting harmonic motion.&lt;SEP&gt;A simple harmonic oscillator is a system consisting of a mass attached to a spring, which oscillates about an equilibrium point due to the restoring force exerted by the spring.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-201ad2bff594c69ddcdebbbde0310588&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2281e4b3e341841f3ab4fc1ff9c7a634&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-284988f822bbc861f6935dafb7bde2c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fe015f4be9f2111ba91f577393b86cd</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Inputs (u1, u2)">
  <data key="d0">Inputs (u1, u2)</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Inputs u1 and u2 are external forces or signals applied to the mechanical system, affecting its behavior.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-201ad2bff594c69ddcdebbbde0310588</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Outputs (y1, y2)">
  <data key="d0">Outputs (y1, y2)</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Outputs y1 and y2 are the responses or results of the mechanical system's dynamics.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-201ad2bff594c69ddcdebbbde0310588</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
