</node>
<node id="DC Servomotor System">
  <data key="d0">DC Servomotor System</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">A DC servomotor system is a mechanical or electrical system that includes a motor driving a load, with components like moment of inertia, torque, and gear ratio.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-eae6e7cf7c375d236da8e4fd6f746d02</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Mathematical Modeling of Fluid Systems and Thermal Systems">
  <data key="d0">Mathematical Modeling of Fluid Systems and Thermal Systems</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">This category involves creating mathematical models to describe the behavior of fluid systems (pneumatic and hydraulic) and thermal systems using concepts like resistance and capacitance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-eae6e7cf7c375d236da8e4fd6f746d02</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Pneumatic Systems">
  <data key="d0">Pneumatic Systems</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Pneumatic Systems are industrial control systems that utilize compressed air or gases for mechanical motion, control, and operation. They are recognized for their explosion-proof nature, simplicity, and ease of maintenance. These systems are characterized by the use of compressible fluids, which result in lower operating pressures and output powers compared to hydraulic systems. Pneumatic systems are commonly employed in automation and production machinery to transmit signals and power. They are integral to the functioning of pneumatic controllers and are used to power tools, convey materials, or control the movement of machines, often through proportional valves. Despite their advantages, pneumatic systems can experience transport lag, which may influence their control response. Overall, Pneumatic Systems are essential components in various industrial applications, providing reliable and efficient solutions for mechanical motion and control.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-131d68e1d8fb1dac5267fbb38c0b52ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30f7b7fbdbec5ce9d814319c46f46972&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eae6e7cf7c375d236da8e4fd6f746d02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8ea5a2f30b2dcfbbb586c6854279bee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b847793aceb37d63da174b89e67a501&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a6b4cd2d53cd90421b101e0434c0e9d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6fde4856c7b2f76783cc1fa6680d81f</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Hydraulic Servo Systems">
  <data key="d0">Hydraulic Servo Systems</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Hydraulic servo systems use fluid power to control machinery, including hydraulic controllers.&lt;SEP&gt;Hydraulic servo systems utilize oil to control machinery, widely employed in machine tools and aircraft control systems.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-eae6e7cf7c375d236da8e4fd6f746d02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30f7b7fbdbec5ce9d814319c46f46972</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Liquid-Level Systems">
  <data key="d0">Liquid-Level Systems</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Liquid-Level Systems refer to systems where tanks interact through various components like pipes, valves, and pumps, affecting fluid flow and control.&lt;SEP&gt;Liquid-level systems are used in process control to manage the level of liquids, incorporating the concepts of resistance and capacitance.&lt;SEP&gt;Liquid-level systems involve the flow of liquids through pipes and tanks, characterized by resistance and capacitance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-eae6e7cf7c375d236da8e4fd6f746d02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30f7b7fbdbec5ce9d814319c46f46972&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a59a135119a827d97b5f3e9ad2c60d59</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Hydraulic Controllers">
  <data key="d0">Hydraulic Controllers</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Hydraulic controllers are devices used to manage hydraulic systems, ensuring precise control over machinery.&lt;SEP&gt;Hydraulic controllers are devices used within hydraulic servo systems to manage fluid power.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-eae6e7cf7c375d236da8e4fd6f746d02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30f7b7fbdbec5ce9d814319c46f46972</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Pneumatic Controllers">
  <data key="d0">Pneumatic Controllers</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Pneumatic controllers are devices used to control pneumatic systems, converting compressed air energy into mechanical energy.&lt;SEP&gt;Pneumatic controllers are devices used to regulate and manage pneumatic systems.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-eae6e7cf7c375d236da8e4fd6f746d02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30f7b7fbdbec5ce9d814319c46f46972</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Laminar Flow">
  <data key="d0">Laminar Flow</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Laminar flow is characterized by smooth, orderly fluid motion in streamlines, represented by linear differential equations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-30f7b7fbdbec5ce9d814319c46f46972</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Turbulent Flow">
  <data key="d0">Turbulent Flow</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Turbulent flow involves chaotic, irregular fluid motion, typically represented by nonlinear differential equations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-30f7b7fbdbec5ce9d814319c46f46972</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Reynolds Number">
  <data key="d0">Reynolds Number</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The Reynolds number is a dimensionless number used to predict flow regimes, distinguishing between laminar and turbulent flow.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-30f7b7fbdbec5ce9d814319c46f46972</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Flow Regimes">
  <data key="d0">Flow Regimes</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Flow regimes refer to the classification of fluid flow as either laminar or turbulent based on the Reynolds number.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-30f7b7fbdbec5ce9d814319c46f46972</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
