<node id="Point P">
  <data key="d0">Point P</data>
  <data key="d1">geo</data>
  <data key="d2">A specific point in the complex plane where the value of K is calculated as 8.9801.&lt;SEP&gt;Point P is a specific location marked on a graph, positioned in the Re-Im plane at approximately (0.5, 1), used to illustrate concepts related to complex numbers.&lt;SEP&gt;Point P is located at coordinates (2, 0) on the real axis of the complex number plane.&lt;SEP&gt;Point P is the steady-state operating point on the head-versus-flow-rate curve.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1bb1a7cabc0b2949b63a14380bfcba5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b52720f9a7352e99f41bd87710c52e0f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59a053a060eb4f14d77b34ae1061cace&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f86521265de1eaaef568da798d2e3a53</data>
