</node>
<node id="Tank">
  <data key="d0">Tank</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">A tank in a liquid-level system, characterized by its capacitance and cross-sectional area.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1bb1a7cabc0b2949b63a14380bfcba5f</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Resistance R_t">
  <data key="d0">Resistance R_t</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The turbulent-flow resistance, R_t, measures opposition to flow in a system.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1bb1a7cabc0b2949b63a14380bfcba5f</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Capacitance C">
  <data key="d0">Capacitance C</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Capacitance C is a measure of the system's ability to store gas, calculated as the derivative of mass with respect to pressure.&lt;SEP&gt;Capacitance C is the change in stored liquid necessary for a unit change in head.&lt;SEP&gt;Capacitance C refers to the property of the tank that determines its ability to store fluid.&lt;SEP&gt;The capacitance of the bellows, affecting the time constants in the pneumatic controller's transfer functions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1bb1a7cabc0b2949b63a14380bfcba5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-14b1ff7bfb2a542970b65ad8cdaa0a75&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5ae34faa3613c5b2f380b5bfb27f630&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e66f9ddf363acc92f98e91b488e76691</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Turbulent-flow Resistance R_t">
  <data key="d0">Turbulent-flow Resistance R_t</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Turbulent-flow resistance R_t is a measure of opposition to flow, dependent on flow rate and head.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1bb1a7cabc0b2949b63a14380bfcba5f</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Flow Rate Q">
  <data key="d0">Flow Rate Q</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Flow rate Q refers to the volume of fluid passing a point per unit time.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1bb1a7cabc0b2949b63a14380bfcba5f</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Head H">
  <data key="d0">Head H</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Head H is a measure of the potential energy level of a fluid in a system.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1bb1a7cabc0b2949b63a14380bfcba5f</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
