<node id="Pipes">
  <data key="d0">Pipes</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Pipes are components connecting different parts of the liquid-level system, facilitating fluid transfer between tanks.&lt;SEP&gt;Pipes are long, hollow tubes in the hydraulic system that facilitate fluid flow between different components.&lt;SEP&gt;Pipes are part of the mechanical system, connected to valves and tubes, facilitating fluid or gas flow.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e8fbd6e1853dfec68a3d5baf7fb35d91&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b604e2ab2b01dde76afde4bf0e414554&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a59a135119a827d97b5f3e9ad2c60d59</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Valves">
  <data key="d0">Valves</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Valves are components used to control the flow of air into or out of a system, operable manually or automatically by an actuator.&lt;SEP&gt;Valves control the flow of fluid within the liquid-level system, with some being open and others closed.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-344b982779dae543f1e2fa4c92c88748&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a59a135119a827d97b5f3e9ad2c60d59</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Pumps">
  <data key="d0">Pumps</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Pumps are used to move fluid within the liquid-level system, connected to the inlet and outlet pipes of the tanks.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a59a135119a827d97b5f3e9ad2c60d59</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Steady-State Flow Rate">
  <data key="d0">Steady-State Flow Rate</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The Steady-State Flow Rate is a constant flow rate in the liquid-level system, represented by the symbol Q.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a59a135119a827d97b5f3e9ad2c60d59</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Steady-State Liquid Level of Tank 1">
  <data key="d0">Steady-State Liquid Level of Tank 1</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The Steady-State Liquid Level of Tank 1 is the constant liquid height in Tank 1, denoted by the symbol H1.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a59a135119a827d97b5f3e9ad2c60d59</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Steady-State Liquid Level of Tank 2">
  <data key="d0">Steady-State Liquid Level of Tank 2</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The Steady-State Liquid Level of Tank 2 is the constant liquid height in Tank 2, denoted by the symbol H2.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a59a135119a827d97b5f3e9ad2c60d59</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Hydraulic Systems">
  <data key="d0">Hydraulic Systems</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Hydraulic systems are mechanical systems that use fluid power to perform work, characterized by high-pressure operation, rapid-acting capabilities, and the ability to develop large forces.&lt;SEP&gt;Hydraulic systems are systems that use incompressible fluids for operation, providing higher pressure and power output compared to pneumatic systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Hydraulic systems involve fluid dynamics and can exhibit transport lag, impacting their control system behavior.&lt;SEP&gt;Hydraulic systems use oil as a fluid, which is incompressible, and are characterized by higher operating pressures and output powers compared to pneumatic systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Systems utilizing hydraulic circuitry for applications requiring high power, precision, and flexibility, such as machine tools and aircraft control systems.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-131d68e1d8fb1dac5267fbb38c0b52ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9200d2e3713c31cbf8dd0e095c6b390b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2c28aabc6197b8bf9c87d2057d278f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a6b4cd2d53cd90421b101e0434c0e9d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6fde4856c7b2f76783cc1fa6680d81f</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Equation (4–7)">
  <data key="d0">Equation (4–7)</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Equation (4–7) represents the transfer function of an interacted system obtained through block diagram reduction.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a6b4cd2d53cd90421b101e0434c0e9d1</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Figure 4–3">
  <data key="d0">Figure 4–3</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Figure 4–3 displays the block diagram of a system, showing successive simplifications leading to a final equivalent representation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a6b4cd2d53cd90421b101e0434c0e9d1</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Proportional Controllers">
  <data key="d0">Proportional Controllers</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Proportional controllers are devices used in control systems to maintain desired output by adjusting control inputs based on the difference between the setpoint and the measured process variable.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f6fde4856c7b2f76783cc1fa6680d81f</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Pressure Systems">
  <data key="d0">Pressure Systems</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Pressure systems involve the flow of gas through pipelines and pressure vessels, characterized by resistance and capacitance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f6fde4856c7b2f76783cc1fa6680d81f</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Pressure System">
  <data key="d0">Pressure System</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">A pressure system involves the dynamics of gas pressure, volume, and flow within a vessel, often analyzed using principles of thermodynamics.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-449bed3c4cecf8b0bddf9a7ce769394b</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Ideal Gas Law">
  <data key="d0">Ideal Gas Law</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The Ideal Gas Law is a fundamental equation in thermodynamics that relates pressure, volume, and temperature of an ideal gas.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-449bed3c4cecf8b0bddf9a7ce769394b</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Polytropic Process">
  <data key="d0">Polytropic Process</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">A polytropic process is a thermodynamic process that follows a specific heat transfer path, characterized by a polytropic exponent.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-449bed3c4cecf8b0bddf9a7ce769394b</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Gas Pressure">
  <data key="d0">Gas Pressure</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Gas pressure is the force exerted by gas molecules against the walls of its container, measured in lb_f/ft^2.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-449bed3c4cecf8b0bddf9a7ce769394b</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Volume of Vessel">
  <data key="d0">Volume of Vessel</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The volume of vessel refers to the space within a container that holds gas, measured in cubic feet.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-449bed3c4cecf8b0bddf9a7ce769394b</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Density">
  <data key="d0">Density</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Density is a property of the fluid, assumed constant, affecting flow and displacement equations.&lt;SEP&gt;Density is the mass per unit volume of a substance, measured in lb/ft^3.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-449bed3c4cecf8b0bddf9a7ce769394b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da45ed46b3417493dc6e2a6d545bd8ed</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Universal Gas Constant">
  <data key="d0">Universal Gas Constant</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The universal gas constant is a physical constant used in equations relating to ideal gases.&lt;SEP&gt;Universal Gas Constant is a physical constant used in equations of state for gases.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-449bed3c4cecf8b0bddf9a7ce769394b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76155cfacd298ba99866d06587bc0e7d</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Specific Volume">
  <data key="d0">Specific Volume</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Specific volume is the volume occupied by a unit mass of a substance, measured in ft^3/lb.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-449bed3c4cecf8b0bddf9a7ce769394b</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Molecular Weight">
  <data key="d0">Molecular Weight</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Molecular weight is the mass of a given molecule, measured in lb/lb-mole.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-449bed3c4cecf8b0bddf9a7ce769394b</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Specific Heat at Constant Pressure">
  <data key="d0">Specific Heat at Constant Pressure</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Specific heat at constant pressure is the heat capacity of a substance when pressure is constant.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-449bed3c4cecf8b0bddf9a7ce769394b</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Specific Heat at Constant Volume">
  <data key="d0">Specific Heat at Constant Volume</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Specific heat at constant volume is the heat capacity of a substance when volume is constant.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-449bed3c4cecf8b0bddf9a7ce769394b</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Pneumatic Nozzle–Flapper Amplifier">
  <data key="d0">Pneumatic Nozzle–Flapper Amplifier</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">A pneumatic device that converts small changes in the position of the flapper into large changes in back pressure, allowing for controlled power output.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e66f9ddf363acc92f98e91b488e76691</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Flapper">
  <data key="d0">Flapper</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The flapper is a crucial component in pneumatic control systems, specifically within pneumatic controllers, that plays a vital role in regulating pressure. It is a small metal piece that interacts with the nozzle, moving back and forth in response to pressure changes. This movement affects the nozzle back pressure, which is essential for the operation of the pneumatic nozzle–flapper amplifier. The flapper operates within the force-balance type controller, adjusting its movement based on error signals and feedback bellows, thereby exerting force as part of the air supply system.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2ade22120b73dcc1eb2fff81533ae0bd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e29b944093645b10134bb068a0e85609&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-243f218034c813f63a13349f4953ce1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-feef65cbaf78b28598f6c9d649127cbd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d9ad31b90878cd9ce75a3c06dde5440&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e66f9ddf363acc92f98e91b488e76691</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Nozzle">
  <data key="d0">Nozzle</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The nozzle is a crucial component in pneumatic systems, serving multiple functions that influence airflow and pressure control. It directs airflow and interacts with the flapper, playing a key role in controlling pressure within pneumatic controllers. Within such systems, the nozzle is where back pressure changes occur, significantly affecting control pressure. It focuses high-pressure air onto surfaces, which is essential in applications such as painting or cutting, by creating force. Additionally, the nozzle is part of the force-balance type controller, allowing air to escape to the atmosphere. Positioned at the top of the system diagram, it is responsible for regulating the pressure at which compressed air exits the system.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2ade22120b73dcc1eb2fff81533ae0bd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-243f218034c813f63a13349f4953ce1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-618d28373e3d4b10e2bb1e5daa8b83e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-feef65cbaf78b28598f6c9d649127cbd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d9ad31b90878cd9ce75a3c06dde5440&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e66f9ddf363acc92f98e91b488e76691</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Orifice">
  <data key="d0">Orifice</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">A component in the control system diagram, represented by a rectangular box with arrows indicating fluid flow.&lt;SEP&gt;A small opening through which air flows, essential for regulating air supply in the pneumatic system.&lt;SEP&gt;An orifice is a narrow opening that restricts the flow of air through it, typically used in pneumatic systems to control airflow.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-344b982779dae543f1e2fa4c92c88748&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db868c08afc68de9d8850f06c963dfd1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e66f9ddf363acc92f98e91b488e76691</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Air Supply">
  <data key="d0">Air Supply</data>
  <data key="d1">equipment</data>
  <data key="d2">The Air Supply provides the compressed air necessary for the operation of the pneumatic valve system.&lt;SEP&gt;The source of compressed air that powers the pneumatic system, ensuring constant pressure for operation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-618d28373e3d4b10e2bb1e5daa8b83e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e66f9ddf363acc92f98e91b488e76691</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Input Valve">
  <data key="d0">Input Valve</data>
  <data key="d1">equipment</data>
  <data key="d2">Regulates the flow of air from the air supply to the control valve, maintaining system pressure.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e66f9ddf363acc92f98e91b488e76691</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Control Valve">
  <data key="d0">Control Valve</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">A component that adjusts the pressure of air supplied to the nozzle, playing a critical role in regulating airflow and generating force.&lt;SEP&gt;Adjusts the pressure of air supplied to the nozzle, crucial for controlling the pneumatic system.&lt;SEP&gt;Control Valve regulates fluid flow into the chamber based on the pressure difference between reference and output pressures.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2ade22120b73dcc1eb2fff81533ae0bd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-243f218034c813f63a13349f4953ce1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e66f9ddf363acc92f98e91b488e76691</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Resistance R">
  <data key="d0">Resistance R</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Resistance R is a constant value derived from the pressure difference divided by the gas flow rate, used in the analysis of pressure systems.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e66f9ddf363acc92f98e91b488e76691</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Pressure Change dp">
  <data key="d0">Pressure Change dp</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Pressure change dp refers to small variations in pressure within the system, affecting the operation of pneumatic devices.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e66f9ddf363acc92f98e91b488e76691</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Nozzle Back Pressure Pb">
  <data key="d0">Nozzle Back Pressure Pb</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Nozzle back pressure Pb is the pressure in the nozzle influenced by the nozzle-flapper distance and supply pressure.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e66f9ddf363acc92f98e91b488e76691</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Supply Pressure Ps">
  <data key="d0">Supply Pressure Ps</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Supply pressure Ps is the constant pressure provided by the air supply to power the pneumatic system.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e66f9ddf363acc92f98e91b488e76691</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Ambient Pressure Pa">
  <data key="d0">Ambient Pressure Pa</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Ambient pressure Pa is the lowest possible pressure in the system, typically the surrounding atmospheric pressure.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e66f9ddf363acc92f98e91b488e76691</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Pneumatic Relay">
  <data key="d0">Pneumatic Relay</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">A device used in pneumatic controllers to amplify power, capable of handling large airflow quantities.&lt;SEP&gt;Pneumatic relay refers to a type of relay used in pneumatic systems, available in bleed and nonbleed types, and can be reverse acting.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-92ba5cf628b31de1be548cfeea5e1e5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-243f218034c813f63a13349f4953ce1b</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Bleed-Type Relay">
  <data key="d0">Bleed-Type Relay</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">A type of relay where air continues to bleed into the atmosphere even after equilibrium is reached.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-243f218034c813f63a13349f4953ce1b</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Nonbleed-Type Relay">
  <data key="d0">Nonbleed-Type Relay</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">A relay that stops air bleed at equilibrium, preventing pressurized air loss during steady-state operation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-243f218034c813f63a13349f4953ce1b</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Pneumatic Valve System (a)">
  <data key="d0">Pneumatic Valve System (a)</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">A system comprising components like nozzle back pressure, air supply, and pneumatic valve, connected to the atmosphere.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-243f218034c813f63a13349f4953ce1b</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Pneumatic Valve System (b)">
  <data key="d0">Pneumatic Valve System (b)</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">A system similar to (a) but with different relay configurations for controlling air supply and pressure.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-243f218034c813f63a13349f4953ce1b</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Pressure of Air Supplied (Pb)">
  <data key="d0">Pressure of Air Supplied (Pb)</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The pressure of air supplied to the control valve, influencing the force exerted by the flapper.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-243f218034c813f63a13349f4953ce1b</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Pressure of Air Exiting (Pa)">
  <data key="d0">Pressure of Air Exiting (Pa)</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The pressure of air exiting the nozzle, relevant to the operation of the pneumatic system.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-243f218034c813f63a13349f4953ce1b</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Force Exerted by Flapper (Fs)">
  <data key="d0">Force Exerted by Flapper (Fs)</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The force exerted by the flapper, which varies based on air pressure.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-243f218034c813f63a13349f4953ce1b</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Schematic Diagram">
  <data key="d0">Schematic Diagram</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">A technical illustration showing the components and operation of pneumatic systems.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-243f218034c813f63a13349f4953ce1b</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Pneumatic Valve System">
  <data key="d0">Pneumatic Valve System</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The Pneumatic Valve System is a mechanism designed to control airflow between an air supply and the atmosphere, featuring a nozzle, spring-actuated valve, and ports connected to either the atmosphere or a pneumatic system.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-618d28373e3d4b10e2bb1e5daa8b83e8</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Pneumatic Valve">
  <data key="d0">Pneumatic Valve</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The Pneumatic Valve is a central component in the system, controlling the pressure at which compressed air enters and exits the pneumatic system.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-618d28373e3d4b10e2bb1e5daa8b83e8</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Back Pressure">
  <data key="d0">Back Pressure</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Back Pressure is a component that works with the nozzle and pneumatic valve to control the overall pressure of compressed air in the system.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-618d28373e3d4b10e2bb1e5daa8b83e8</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Reverse-Acting Relay">
  <data key="d0">Reverse-Acting Relay</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The Reverse-Acting Relay is a type of pneumatic relay where increased nozzle back pressure forces the ball valve toward the lower seat, decreasing control pressure.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-618d28373e3d4b10e2bb1e5daa8b83e8</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Pneumatic Proportional Controllers">
  <data key="d0">Pneumatic Proportional Controllers</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Pneumatic Proportional Controllers are devices used in industry to regulate pneumatic circuits, including force-distance and force-balance types.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-618d28373e3d4b10e2bb1e5daa8b83e8</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Atmosphere">
  <data key="d0">Atmosphere</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Atmosphere serves as the source of reference pressure in the pressure control system, providing a constant pressure for comparison with output pressure.&lt;SEP&gt;The Atmosphere is the external environment to which air is released or from which it is redirected in the pneumatic valve system.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2ade22120b73dcc1eb2fff81533ae0bd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-618d28373e3d4b10e2bb1e5daa8b83e8</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Force-Distance Type">
  <data key="d0">Force-Distance Type</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The Force-Distance Type is a type of pneumatic proportional controller that uses the distance between components to regulate pressure.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-618d28373e3d4b10e2bb1e5daa8b83e8</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Force-Balance Type">
  <data key="d0">Force-Balance Type</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The Force-Balance Type is a type of pneumatic proportional controller that maintains equilibrium between forces to regulate pressure.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-618d28373e3d4b10e2bb1e5daa8b83e8</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Pneumatic Amplifier">
  <data key="d0">Pneumatic Amplifier</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">A device used in control systems to amplify pneumatic signals for precise control actions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-feef65cbaf78b28598f6c9d649127cbd</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Feedback Bellows">
  <data key="d0">Feedback Bellows</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">A part of the control system that provides feedback by moving the flapper based on pressure changes.&lt;SEP&gt;Component of a pneumatic controller that senses pressure changes and provides feedback to the system.&lt;SEP&gt;Feedback bellows reduce the sensitivity of pneumatic controllers by counteracting the movement initiated by error signals.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-feef65cbaf78b28598f6c9d649127cbd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e29b944093645b10134bb068a0e85609&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b285f50932bff8d3ec6715415855398</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Diaphragm Valve">
  <data key="d0">Diaphragm Valve</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">A valve that controls pressure by moving in response to changes in nozzle back pressure.&lt;SEP&gt;Diaphragm valves are used in pneumatic controllers to regulate flow, opening or closing based on pressure changes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-feef65cbaf78b28598f6c9d649127cbd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e29b944093645b10134bb068a0e85609</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Pneumatic Relay Valve">
  <data key="d0">Pneumatic Relay Valve</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">A valve that uses pneumatic signals to control the flow of air or gas in a system.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-feef65cbaf78b28598f6c9d649127cbd</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Control Pressure">
  <data key="d0">Control Pressure</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Control pressure refers to the pressure exerted in a pneumatic system to control the movement of valves and other components.&lt;SEP&gt;The pressure applied within the pneumatic controller that influences the operation of bellows and flapper movement.&lt;SEP&gt;The pressure output regulated by the diaphragm valve to achieve desired system performance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-feef65cbaf78b28598f6c9d649127cbd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de8767d6e1a854115045ae33d4513569&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d9ad31b90878cd9ce75a3c06dde5440</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Nozzle Back Pressure">
  <data key="d0">Nozzle Back Pressure</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The pressure in the nozzle that is influenced by the position of the flapper and affects system control.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-feef65cbaf78b28598f6c9d649127cbd</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Equilibrium State">
  <data key="d0">Equilibrium State</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Equilibrium State refers to the condition where a system is stable, with all roots of its characteristic equation having negative real parts.&lt;SEP&gt;The equilibrium state refers to the condition where the system's state vector x is zero, indicating stability.&lt;SEP&gt;The state where all variables in the system are balanced, with no net changes occurring.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-feef65cbaf78b28598f6c9d649127cbd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d4f87e9dd3cfeb7f1869f4f209585ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd576c10a0963ba5c33eef163a461a22</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Bellows">
  <data key="d0">Bellows</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">A flexible component in the air compressor system that expands and contracts to compress or release air.&lt;SEP&gt;Bellows are components in the hydraulic system that interact with valves and pipes to regulate fluid flow.&lt;SEP&gt;Bellows in pneumatic controllers act like springs, providing stiffness through their corrugated sides and affecting the system's sensitivity.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e8fbd6e1853dfec68a3d5baf7fb35d91&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e29b944093645b10134bb068a0e85609&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-026e0fcd969517dd30ca84cdf6678f77</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Force-Balance Type Controller">
  <data key="d0">Force-Balance Type Controller</data>
  <data key="d1">equipment</data>
  <data key="d2">A force-balance type controller is a pneumatic controller that uses pressure signals to operate, minimizing mechanical linkages and friction.&lt;SEP&gt;Force-Balance Type Controller is a pneumatic system that regulates pressure using components like a flapper, nozzle, and orifices.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2ade22120b73dcc1eb2fff81533ae0bd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e29b944093645b10134bb068a0e85609</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Pressure Control System">
  <data key="d0">Pressure Control System</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">A system depicted in the diagrams, likely related to fluid dynamics or thermodynamics, featuring various components and labels.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e29b944093645b10134bb068a0e85609</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
