</node>
<node id="Reference Input Pressure">
  <data key="d0">Reference Input Pressure</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Reference Input Pressure is the signal controlling the output pressure, connected to the atmosphere through a valve or flow control device.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2ade22120b73dcc1eb2fff81533ae0bd</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Output Pressure">
  <data key="d0">Output Pressure</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Output Pressure is the controlled variable in the system, measured and compared to the reference pressure to ensure proper system function.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2ade22120b73dcc1eb2fff81533ae0bd</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Chamber">
  <data key="d0">Chamber</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Chamber is the component where fluid accumulates under pressure, with pressure measured by a sensor.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2ade22120b73dcc1eb2fff81533ae0bd</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Orifices">
  <data key="d0">Orifices</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Orifices are openings in the force-balance type controller that influence air flow and pressure regulation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2ade22120b73dcc1eb2fff81533ae0bd</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Pneumatic Actuating Valve">
  <data key="d0">Pneumatic Actuating Valve</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">A pneumatic actuating valve is a device used in pneumatic control systems, known for providing large power outputs and requiring pressurized air for operation.&lt;SEP&gt;A pneumatic actuating valve is a device used to control fluid flow, characterized by its schematic diagram and operational principles involving pressure and valve-stem displacement.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4e1022912f84674a869a68f2ad49c48a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de8767d6e1a854115045ae33d4513569</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Diaphragm">
  <data key="d0">Diaphragm</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The diaphragm in a pneumatic actuating valve is a flexible membrane that responds to changes in pneumatic pressure to control valve displacement.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-de8767d6e1a854115045ae33d4513569</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Pneumatic Controls">
  <data key="d0">Pneumatic Controls</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Pneumatic controls refer to systems that use compressed air to transmit and control energy, often employing pneumatic actuating valves.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-de8767d6e1a854115045ae33d4513569</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Valve Displacement">
  <data key="d0">Valve Displacement</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Valve displacement refers to the movement of the valve stem in response to changes in control pressure in a pneumatic system.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-de8767d6e1a854115045ae33d4513569</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Valve Positioner">
  <data key="d0">Valve Positioner</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">A valve positioner is used to enhance the performance of pneumatic actuating valves by improving control accuracy and reducing hysteresis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4e1022912f84674a869a68f2ad49c48a</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Derivative Control Action">
  <data key="d0">Derivative Control Action</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Derivative Control Action is a control method that uses the rate of change of the error signal to adjust system inputs.&lt;SEP&gt;Derivative Control Action is a control method that uses the rate of change of the error signal to improve system performance, often combined with other control actions.&lt;SEP&gt;Derivative control action is a method for obtaining desired control responses in systems by manipulating transfer functions within feedback paths.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4e1022912f84674a869a68f2ad49c48a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-faf6d229bd33d9a677ddb2c4f3fe8552&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5f3d1f90ecef2ea0c231698609f06418</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Control System Block Diagram">
  <data key="d0">Control System Block Diagram</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The Control System Block Diagram is a comprehensive graphical representation used to analyze and design feedback control systems. It illustrates the flow of signals and the interactions between various components, such as controllers, plants, sensors, and feedback paths. Key components typically depicted in the diagram include input, controller, plant, output, summing junctions, integrators, and transfer functions. The diagram also showcases the system's architecture with elements like transfer functions G(s) and H(s), reference input R(s), and closed-loop response C(s). This visual tool is essential for understanding and designing the relationships and interactions within control systems.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f104d09d0c472d244729f4c0273b66e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37fb7998dd9fe418c1b904b5fad6ac47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a599688f3c870bb8d72b6239047bad9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c317b9ff2b2110c0c0b14f7d7fbc89c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d1c6b6475b03e27e6db3ac883a90115c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4e1022912f84674a869a68f2ad49c48a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-35afe3e90a1acbe01560dbd9ac0de547</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Pneumatic Proportional Controller">
  <data key="d0">Pneumatic Proportional Controller</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">A pneumatic proportional controller is a device depicted in a schematic diagram, used for controlling mechanical systems with proportional control action.&lt;SEP&gt;A type of control system that uses pneumatic signals to perform proportional control of a process.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4e1022912f84674a869a68f2ad49c48a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b285f50932bff8d3ec6715415855398</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Transfer Function H(s)">
  <data key="d0">Transfer Function H(s)</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">H(s) is a transfer function block modeling the dynamics of the plant or process being controlled, influencing the closed-loop response C(s).&lt;SEP&gt;Transfer function H(s) is a fixed component in the system described.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4e1022912f84674a869a68f2ad49c48a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-808fea3f1de10aeed968f879a46b012d</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Reference Input R(s)">
  <data key="d0">Reference Input R(s)</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">R(s) is the reference or setpoint input of the control system, representing the desired value for the system to track.&lt;SEP&gt;Reference Input R(s) is the desired input signal to the control system that guides the output behavior.&lt;SEP&gt;The Reference Input R(s) specifies the desired output of the plant within the control system.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4e1022912f84674a869a68f2ad49c48a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28ae81c40745842e3e00aecec87aa63f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2350dc025ef445f345d067152812c1c9</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Closed-Loop Response C(s)">
  <data key="d0">Closed-Loop Response C(s)</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">C(s) is the actual output of the control system, resulting from the combination of controller G(s) and plant H(s).</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4e1022912f84674a869a68f2ad49c48a</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Pneumatic Proportional-Plus-Derivative Controller">
  <data key="d0">Pneumatic Proportional-Plus-Derivative Controller</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">An advanced control system that incorporates both proportional and derivative actions to enhance control response.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9b285f50932bff8d3ec6715415855398</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Nozzle-Flapper System">
  <data key="d0">Nozzle-Flapper System</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">A mechanism within the pneumatic controller that regulates flow and pressure by adjusting the distance between the nozzle and the flapper.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9b285f50932bff8d3ec6715415855398</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Flowchart Diagram">
  <data key="d0">Flowchart Diagram</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">A diagrammatic representation of processes or information flow, using interconnected boxes and arrows.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9b285f50932bff8d3ec6715415855398</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Graphs with Patterns">
  <data key="d0">Graphs with Patterns</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Visual representations of data with varying patterns, such as oscillating and gradual slopes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9b285f50932bff8d3ec6715415855398</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Restriction R">
  <data key="d0">Restriction R</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">A component in the feedback path of the controller that momentarily prevents the feedback bellows from sensing pressure changes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9b285f50932bff8d3ec6715415855398</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Control Pressure (Pc)">
  <data key="d0">Control Pressure (Pc)</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The pressure within the controller system that is adjusted based on feedback and control actions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9b285f50932bff8d3ec6715415855398</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Actuating Error (e)">
  <data key="d0">Actuating Error (e)</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The error signal in the controller system that initiates changes in control action.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9b285f50932bff8d3ec6715415855398</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Nozzle-Flapper Distance (x)">
  <data key="d0">Nozzle-Flapper Distance (x)</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The distance between the nozzle and flapper, which influences control pressure and system response.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9b285f50932bff8d3ec6715415855398</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Pneumatic Proportional-Plus-Integral Controller">
  <data key="d0">Pneumatic Proportional-Plus-Integral Controller</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">A pneumatic controller that combines proportional control with integral control, modifying the control action to achieve desired system behavior.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3d9ad31b90878cd9ce75a3c06dde5440</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Bellows I">
  <data key="d0">Bellows I</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">A component in the pneumatic controller connected directly to the control pressure source, responsible for initial pressure changes.&lt;SEP&gt;A component in the pneumatic controller that experiences pressure changes due to control pressure.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e5ae34faa3613c5b2f380b5bfb27f630&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d9ad31b90878cd9ce75a3c06dde5440</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Bellows II">
  <data key="d0">Bellows II</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">A component in the pneumatic controller connected through a restriction, allowing for pressure changes over time to achieve integral control action.&lt;SEP&gt;Another component in the pneumatic controller, similar to Bellows I, experiencing pressure changes via series resistances.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e5ae34faa3613c5b2f380b5bfb27f630&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d9ad31b90878cd9ce75a3c06dde5440</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Technical Diagram">
  <data key="d0">Technical Diagram</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">A diagram featuring sections with symbols, boxes, lines, and arrows that convey information about processes or systems, related to engineering or physics.&lt;SEP&gt;A visual representation comprising sections with circuit diagrams, block diagrams, and graphical data related to engineering concepts.&lt;SEP&gt;The technical diagram provides a detailed illustration of the mechanical system's components and their interconnections, using symbols to convey dynamic properties.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c9ba0b5a3e032183793285284f3603fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9200d2e3713c31cbf8dd0e095c6b390b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d9ad31b90878cd9ce75a3c06dde5440</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Integral Control Action">
  <data key="d0">Integral Control Action</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">A control action that cancels the feedback provided by proportional control, allowing for continuous adjustment over time.&lt;SEP&gt;Integral Control Action is a control method that eliminates steady-state error by integrating the error signal over time, potentially leading to oscillatory responses.&lt;SEP&gt;Integral Control Action refers to the method of control produced by the hydraulic jet-pipe controller, characterized by its transfer function.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-694a931017660524799c6054826da2a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5f3d1f90ecef2ea0c231698609f06418&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d9ad31b90878cd9ce75a3c06dde5440</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Pneumatic Proportional-Plus-Integral-Plus-Derivative Controller">
  <data key="d0">Pneumatic Proportional-Plus-Integral-Plus-Derivative Controller</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">A type of controller that combines pneumatic control with proportional, integral, and derivative actions to manage processes or systems.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9200d2e3713c31cbf8dd0e095c6b390b</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Pc">
  <data key="d0">Pc</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">A label used in the diagram, possibly representing a specific pressure or control variable in the context of pneumatic systems.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9200d2e3713c31cbf8dd0e095c6b390b</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Ri">
  <data key="d0">Ri</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">A label used in the diagram, possibly representing a resistance or input variable in the context of the control systems.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9200d2e3713c31cbf8dd0e095c6b390b</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Hydraulic Actuators">
  <data key="d0">Hydraulic Actuators</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Hydraulic actuators are components of hydraulic systems that convert fluid power into mechanical motion, offering flexibility in design with both linear and rotary options.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f2c28aabc6197b8bf9c87d2057d278f8</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Hydraulic Servo System">
  <data key="d0">Hydraulic Servo System</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">A hydraulic servo system is a type of hydraulic system that uses a pilot-valve-controlled hydraulic power amplifier and actuator for precise control of large power outputs.&lt;SEP&gt;The Hydraulic Servo System is a mechanical system that includes components such as valves, pumps, and pipes to facilitate fluid flow.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f2c28aabc6197b8bf9c87d2057d278f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-87477e7fcde631f4167b68d49ae5e3bc</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Hydraulic Fluid">
  <data key="d0">Hydraulic Fluid</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Hydraulic Fluid is the medium used in the hydraulic system, ejected from the jet pipe to facilitate piston movement.&lt;SEP&gt;Hydraulic fluid is used in hydraulic systems to transfer power, act as a lubricant, and carry away heat.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-694a931017660524799c6054826da2a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2c28aabc6197b8bf9c87d2057d278f8</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Pilot Valve">
  <data key="d0">Pilot Valve</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The Pilot Valve is a four-way valve with two lands on the spool, crucial for controlling oil flow and pressure in hydraulic systems.&lt;SEP&gt;The pilot valve displacement affects the power piston velocity in the liquid-level control system.&lt;SEP&gt;The pilot valve is a component in hydraulic servo systems, controlling large power outputs with minimal power input.&lt;SEP&gt;The pilot valve is part of the hydraulic controller system, controlling oil flow and interacting with the feedback link.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fdb46bdfea03c8ad1daae623cf71c4a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f3d0206ddf0a9d09a9dfc373b545bef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2c28aabc6197b8bf9c87d2057d278f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b604e2ab2b01dde76afde4bf0e414554</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Dither Signal">
  <data key="d0">Dither Signal</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">A dither signal is a high-frequency signal of small amplitude used to improve the sensitivity and linearity of hydraulic servomotors.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f2c28aabc6197b8bf9c87d2057d278f8</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Valve Orifice Area">
  <data key="d0">Valve Orifice Area</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The Valve Orifice Area refers to the specific regions in a valve where fluid flow occurs, defined by areas A1, A2, A3, and A4.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-87477e7fcde631f4167b68d49ae5e3bc</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Power Cylinder">
  <data key="d0">Power Cylinder</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The Power Cylinder is a component in the hydraulic system that contains a large piston, creating a hydraulic force to move a load.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-87477e7fcde631f4167b68d49ae5e3bc</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Flow Rates">
  <data key="d0">Flow Rates</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Flow Rates refer to the measurement of fluid passing through valve orifices, denoted as q1, q2, q3, and q4.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-87477e7fcde631f4167b68d49ae5e3bc</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Linearization Technique">
  <data key="d0">Linearization Technique</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The Linearization Technique is a method used to obtain a linearized mathematical model of the hydraulic servomotor.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-87477e7fcde631f4167b68d49ae5e3bc</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Valve">
  <data key="d0">Valve</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Valve is a versatile component used in various systems to control the flow of fluids. It is often denoted by the symbol 'V' in mechanical system diagrams and plays a crucial role in directing fluid flow. In the air compressor system, the valve regulates the flow of air, while in the conical water-tank system, it manages the flow of water, impacting both the head and flow rate. Within hydraulic systems, the valve is essential for controlling the flow of fluid, including oil, and is connected to smaller pipes labeled '1' and '2' to facilitate fluid movement. It allows for adjustments in speed and direction when controlling fluid flow to a motor. The valve's design can be symmetrical, affecting flow rates and pressure distribution, and it comes in various types, such as overlapped and underlapped, to accommodate different sensitivity levels. Overall, valves are indispensable in managing fluid dynamics across multiple mechanical and hydraulic systems.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-87477e7fcde631f4167b68d49ae5e3bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-12881ab3d33126ccd266da1257ad2563&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ec9bff7736610bd695d1b222222e6f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-026e0fcd969517dd30ca84cdf6678f77&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76155cfacd298ba99866d06587bc0e7d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-694a931017660524799c6054826da2a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db868c08afc68de9d8850f06c963dfd1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fdb46bdfea03c8ad1daae623cf71c4a1</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Piston">
  <data key="d0">Piston</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">A component that moves within the cylinder to compress or release air in the air compressor system.&lt;SEP&gt;A cylindrical component with a hole in the center, connected to a spring and part of a larger system.&lt;SEP&gt;A mechanical component exerting force on the mass, connected to a pressure source in the diagram.&lt;SEP&gt;The Piston is a part of the power cylinder, moved by hydraulic force to exert pressure and facilitate mechanical work.&lt;SEP&gt;The piston is a component in the system whose displacement is influenced by forces such as spring force and pressure differences.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-45a3caf311e2ab85a8b8795fbe5c9365&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f9976290aaf5bc6b5c7806f43bcf303&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-87477e7fcde631f4167b68d49ae5e3bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da45ed46b3417493dc6e2a6d545bd8ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-026e0fcd969517dd30ca84cdf6678f77</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Return Pressure">
  <data key="d0">Return Pressure</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Return Pressure refers to the pressure in the return line, assumed to be small and negligible in the analysis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-87477e7fcde631f4167b68d49ae5e3bc</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Ports">
  <data key="d0">Ports</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Ports are openings in the valve orifice area, defined as ports 1, 2, 3, and 4, through which fluid flows.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-87477e7fcde631f4167b68d49ae5e3bc</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Fluid">
  <data key="d0">Fluid</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The fluid in the analysis is assumed to be incompressible, impacting the dynamics of the valve system.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9ec9bff7736610bd695d1b222222e6f0</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Power Piston">
  <data key="d0">Power Piston</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The Power Piston is a crucial mechanical component within hydraulic systems, specifically designed to convert hydraulic force into motion. It operates by responding to pressure differences, which are influenced by the displacement of the jet nozzle. This movement is essential for facilitating the operation of hydraulic servomotors. Within these systems, the power piston affects the load mass and friction by moving in response to fluid pressure changes. Additionally, it plays a significant role in influencing the feedback link and pilot valve actions, as its velocity is proportional to the pilot-valve displacement in liquid-level control systems. Furthermore, the power piston receives signals from the hydraulic controller to adjust the engine's fuel valve opening, showcasing its integral function in various hydraulic applications.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-45a3caf311e2ab85a8b8795fbe5c9365&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b604e2ab2b01dde76afde4bf0e414554&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ec9bff7736610bd695d1b222222e6f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-694a931017660524799c6054826da2a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f3d0206ddf0a9d09a9dfc373b545bef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3803a4d9dea32680b8f26e00e4beeb3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fdb46bdfea03c8ad1daae623cf71c4a1</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Pressure Difference (Δp)">
  <data key="d0">Pressure Difference (Δp)</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The pressure difference across the power piston, denoted as Δp, influences the flow rates and valve operation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9ec9bff7736610bd695d1b222222e6f0</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Flow Rate (q)">
  <data key="d0">Flow Rate (q)</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Flow rate (q) refers to the volume of fluid moving through the hydraulic system, affecting the power piston's velocity and system response.&lt;SEP&gt;The flow rate is a function of valve displacement and pressure difference, crucial for system performance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9ec9bff7736610bd695d1b222222e6f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3803a4d9dea32680b8f26e00e4beeb3</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Valve Coefficients (a and b)">
  <data key="d0">Valve Coefficients (a and b)</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Coefficients a and b are parameters that define the linearized model of the valve near an operating point.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9ec9bff7736610bd695d1b222222e6f0</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Spool Valve">
  <data key="d0">Spool Valve</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The spool valve is a component in hydraulic systems that controls fluid flow and pressure, crucial for the operation of hydraulic servomotors.&lt;SEP&gt;The spool valve is central to the system, with its displacement affecting the pressure and flow rate.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9ec9bff7736610bd695d1b222222e6f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3803a4d9dea32680b8f26e00e4beeb3</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Hydraulic Servomotor">
  <data key="d0">Hydraulic Servomotor</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">A hydraulic servomotor is a device that uses fluid pressure to create mechanical movement, often used for precise control in machinery.&lt;SEP&gt;A hydraulic servomotor is a device using fluid pressure to control mechanical load movement, involving components like a pump, motor, valve, and load.&lt;SEP&gt;The Hydraulic Servomotor is a pilot-valve-controlled hydraulic power amplifier and actuator, acting as an integrator or integral controller for hydraulic systems.&lt;SEP&gt;The hydraulic servomotor acts as a proportional controller when a feedback link is added.&lt;SEP&gt;The hydraulic servomotor acts as an integral controller and can be modified to a proportional controller with a feedback link.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-da45ed46b3417493dc6e2a6d545bd8ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b604e2ab2b01dde76afde4bf0e414554&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-344b982779dae543f1e2fa4c92c88748&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f3d0206ddf0a9d09a9dfc373b545bef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3803a4d9dea32680b8f26e00e4beeb3</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Characteristic Curves">
  <data key="d0">Characteristic Curves</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Characteristic curves are graphical representations of the hydraulic servomotor's linearized behavior, showing relationships between variables such as flow rate, displacement, and pressure.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d3803a4d9dea32680b8f26e00e4beeb3</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Load Mass">
  <data key="d0">Load Mass</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Load mass refers to the mass being moved by the power piston, influenced by both the hydraulic force and viscous friction.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d3803a4d9dea32680b8f26e00e4beeb3</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Viscous Friction">
  <data key="d0">Viscous Friction</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">A force opposing motion in the load element, considered in the control system's dynamics.&lt;SEP&gt;Viscous friction is a force that opposes motion in the load element of a control system, affecting its dynamics.&lt;SEP&gt;Viscous friction is a load element in servo systems that impacts the system's resistance and response to motion.&lt;SEP&gt;Viscous friction is the resistance encountered by the power piston due to the viscosity of the fluid, affecting its movement and efficiency.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-39fb7e7ecf98024e40979eb23f0ae0a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e045a2c6fa20bf1beb094683eabf565&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3803a4d9dea32680b8f26e00e4beeb3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd437ba37843beb72e13fcc99049d49c</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Linearized Mathematical Model">
  <data key="d0">Linearized Mathematical Model</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">A linearized mathematical model simplifies complex systems to analyze behavior near a specific operating point, such as the origin in hydraulic systems.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d3803a4d9dea32680b8f26e00e4beeb3</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Piston Area (A)">
  <data key="d0">Piston Area (A)</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Piston area (A) is the surface area of the power piston that interacts with fluid pressure, influencing force and velocity in hydraulic systems.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d3803a4d9dea32680b8f26e00e4beeb3</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Pressure Difference (ΔP)">
  <data key="d0">Pressure Difference (ΔP)</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Pressure difference (ΔP) is the differential pressure applied across the power piston, driving its movement and force generation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d3803a4d9dea32680b8f26e00e4beeb3</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Oil Density (ρ)">
  <data key="d0">Oil Density (ρ)</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Oil density (ρ) is the mass per unit volume of the hydraulic fluid, impacting the force and movement dynamics within the system.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d3803a4d9dea32680b8f26e00e4beeb3</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Hydraulic Integral Controller">
  <data key="d0">Hydraulic Integral Controller</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">A hydraulic integral controller is used to maintain the liquid level in control systems by adjusting the inlet valve based on changes in the head.&lt;SEP&gt;The Hydraulic Integral Controller is a system comprising a pilot-valve-controlled hydraulic power amplifier and actuator, serving as the basis of the hydraulic control circuit.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fdb46bdfea03c8ad1daae623cf71c4a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f3d0206ddf0a9d09a9dfc373b545bef</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Oil">
  <data key="d0">Oil</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Oil is a hydraulic fluid used in servomotors, affecting flow rate, pressure, and system operation.&lt;SEP&gt;Oil under pressure is used in the hydraulic system to generate mechanical motion through pistons and cylinders.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-694a931017660524799c6054826da2a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f3d0206ddf0a9d09a9dfc373b545bef</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Zero-Lapped Valve">
  <data key="d0">Zero-Lapped Valve</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">A Zero-Lapped Valve has a land width identical to the port width, simplifying analyses of hydraulic servomotors.&lt;SEP&gt;Zero-Lapped Valve is a valve design where the spool and valve body edges align, minimizing leakage.&lt;SEP&gt;Zero-lapped valve refers to a type of valve design that aims to improve response characteristics in fluid control systems.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0d107c40e8d19f88e2db4b3ea948e97e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f3d0206ddf0a9d09a9dfc373b545bef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76155cfacd298ba99866d06587bc0e7d</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
