<node id="Graph">
  <data key="d0">Graph</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The Graph is a comprehensive visual representation that encompasses various mathematical and system-related concepts. It depicts the behavior of multiple functions and variables over time, including r(t) and c(t), illustrating their rates of change. The Graph serves as a visual tool to plot complex numbers, showing both real and imaginary components, as well as their magnitude. It features axes and marked points that visually represent system variables and responses, including curves with tangent lines at inflection points to illustrate mathematical concepts related to system responses.

The Graph includes plots with oscillating lines, demonstrating periodic behavior and phase shifts as input values increase. It displays various lines that represent different functions or relationships between decibels (dB) and frequency (ω), as well as a curved line representing an exponential response, complete with mathematical equations and labels indicating specific characteristics such as slope and percentage values.

Additionally, the Graph illustrates resonance and oscillation phenomena, with axes labeled 'Re' and 'Im', and curves indicating frequency components. It shows the response of an initial condition to various input values over time, with axes labeled 'Output' and 't (sec)', and illustrates the unit-ramp response of the system with specific axis labels and data points. The Graph includes a polar plot illustrating the system's pole and zero configurations, and a root-locus plot showing symmetry about the y-axis and the path of poles in the complex plane.

Furthermore, the Graph presents pressure versus flow rate relationships for Valve 1 and Valve 2, allowing for comparison of their performance characteristics. It represents mathematical functions or equations with axes labeled 'c(t)' and 't', featuring curved lines, numerical values, and symbols indicative of a dynamic system or process. The Graph visually represents relationships between variables σ and ω, including lines, labels, and arrows, and describes the response of various variables to an initial condition across six different graphs. Overall, the Graph provides a detailed visual representation of mathematical relationships and system dynamics, showcasing functions and relationships between variables on axes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3a5c8adb826b6a09285fe1ad5b9d9b8c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab1222a4f68b9900993c6bdde861432b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c5e4f7e43e12b75521c4c048c3b222a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a89464a87dc57e95afa0a980ba9d6c0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d2c20fec382eb167929db2080ec8c24&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5d9384ff4d2caf674fcfb9545ee0e6b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95dada5b51e73c98f754b3ae69765f91&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b79361c4f9b3077dd7e1175a33749008&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6970497cbdbb9aab39be9459aa607c48&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-691177b7d933c82cade5a9fd3f182f4a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-602e1bf386d85476513e06ee772f8a95&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56f12da94fdc89592ee91860dba06293&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a12a1fcc8b96ef105600adda81cf5b8f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8fbd6e1853dfec68a3d5baf7fb35d91&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf299ff5c8d29fc06d76cf7459e022b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53900274f2c35aaf0d99d0a9ee95f307&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1196f23376113f0a5fd1445c371198e0</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
