  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="K-Fold Cross-Validation">
  <data key="d0">K-Fold Cross-Validation</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">K-fold cross-validation is a technique that divides the dataset into k subsets, using k-1 subsets for training and one for testing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4e3f6409d4b23a0e16d4df95cc418876</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Holdout Method">
  <data key="d0">Holdout Method</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Holdout method is a simple cross-validation technique where the dataset is split into training and testing sets.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4e3f6409d4b23a0e16d4df95cc418876</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Walk-Forward Optimization">
  <data key="d0">Walk-Forward Optimization</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Walk-forward optimization is a technique used in time series analysis to validate models by training on past data and testing on future data.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4e3f6409d4b23a0e16d4df95cc418876</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Rolling Window">
  <data key="d0">Rolling Window</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Rolling window is a technique used to evaluate models by using a fixed-size window that moves over the dataset for training and testing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4e3f6409d4b23a0e16d4df95cc418876</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
