</node>
<node id="Servo System with Velocity Feedback">
  <data key="d0">Servo System with Velocity Feedback</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">A system that uses the derivative of the output signal to improve performance, often employing a tachometer to avoid noise amplification.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-810cac8c012efc35656f6fae67fff21c</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Tachometer">
  <data key="d0">Tachometer</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">A device used in the Servo System with Velocity Feedback to measure the derivative of the output position signal, helping to improve system performance without amplifying noise.&lt;SEP&gt;A device used to measure the angular velocity of a motor, producing an output proportional to the velocity without the need for differentiation.&lt;SEP&gt;A tachometer is a rate feedback device commonly used in positional servo systems to measure velocity.&lt;SEP&gt;Tachometer is a device used to measure the rotational speed of an object, often used in feedback systems.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-810cac8c012efc35656f6fae67fff21c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d424f9b5c8e1c4caa0b22f889469da1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-caf32671a4ee19f2726367a3b3826926&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76155cfacd298ba99866d06587bc0e7d</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Equation (5-10)">
  <data key="d0">Equation (5-10)</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">A standard equation for a second-order system used to obtain rise time, peak time, maximum overshoot, and settling time.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-810cac8c012efc35656f6fae67fff21c</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Equation (5-12)">
  <data key="d0">Equation (5-12)</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">An equation related to the M_p versus ζ curve, providing insights into system dynamics.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-810cac8c012efc35656f6fae67fff21c</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Velocity Feedback">
  <data key="d0">Velocity Feedback</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">A control strategy involving feedback based on velocity to enhance system performance, used in System III.&lt;SEP&gt;A method in control systems where feedback from the velocity signal is used to improve system performance by increasing the damping ratio.&lt;SEP&gt;Velocity Feedback is a control system mechanism that uses velocity measurements to adjust system performance.&lt;SEP&gt;Velocity feedback is a control mechanism where the feedback signal is proportional to the velocity of the system output.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-577f4c0582663d9533ba9e75104e8038&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c90e64ef4d3ea69c9b12410204a70bfb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-caf32671a4ee19f2726367a3b3826926&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76155cfacd298ba99866d06587bc0e7d</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Damping Ratio (\(\zeta\))">
  <data key="d0">Damping Ratio (\(\zeta\))</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">A dimensionless measure describing how oscillations in a system decay after a disturbance, affecting the shape of frequency-response curves.&lt;SEP&gt;A parameter that indicates how oscillations in a system decay after a disturbance, influenced by velocity feedback.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5c5ea418170c18599f96d1d10d3ce8a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-caf32671a4ee19f2726367a3b3826926</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Undamped Natural Frequency (\(\omega_n\))">
  <data key="d0">Undamped Natural Frequency (\(\omega_n\))</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The frequency at which a system oscillates in the absence of damping, calculated as \(\sqrt{K/J}\).</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-caf32671a4ee19f2726367a3b3826926</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
