  <data key="d0">Equation (5–28)</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Equation (5–28) is used for calculating the time response c(t) for underdamped cases.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c1b12ce7d358a5298c40691eca86f278</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Natural Frequency (ωn)">
  <data key="d0">Natural Frequency (ωn)</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Natural frequency is a parameter that describes the rate at which a system oscillates in the absence of damping.&lt;SEP&gt;Natural frequency refers to the frequency at which a system oscillates when not subjected to external forces, crucial in analyzing system dynamics.&lt;SEP&gt;Natural frequency, ωn, is a parameter that determines the speed of oscillations in a second-order system.&lt;SEP&gt;The natural frequency (ωn) is a parameter that represents the frequency at which a system oscillates naturally without external forces, significant in analyzing polar plots.&lt;SEP&gt;The natural frequency (ωn) is a parameter used in the standard second-order system to describe its oscillatory behavior.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-af7ba33d6c623a912a3380defbe28756&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1b12ce7d358a5298c40691eca86f278&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-535949f72f62ac84bb8daed630bc1653&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a59bbd3f86b4923fd22b10788ad73d53&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-182dc59d89ae078fb7ffb41be064595c</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Unit-Impulse Response Curve">
  <data key="d0">Unit-Impulse Response Curve</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The Unit-Impulse Response Curve represents the system's response to an impulse input, characterized by smooth, continuous lines that start at zero and oscillate about the x-axis.&lt;SEP&gt;The unit-impulse response curve is a graphical representation of how a control system responds to an impulse input over time.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7dee9b6b4fa01e7b310d973887043bfe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a3189f7cb3fb2865b828460dc211a36</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Unit-Step Function Curve">
  <data key="d0">Unit-Step Function Curve</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The Unit-Step Function Curve represents the steady-state response of the system to a constant input, depicted as a step-like graph.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7dee9b6b4fa01e7b310d973887043bfe</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Graph of Curves">
  <data key="d0">Graph of Curves</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">The Graph of Curves event visually illustrates various curves representing unit-impulse and unit-step responses in a dynamic system.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7dee9b6b4fa01e7b310d973887043bfe</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Equation 5-29">
  <data key="d0">Equation 5-29</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Equation 5-29 calculates the maximum overshoot for the unit-impulse response of an underdamped system, involving parameters like damping ratio and natural frequency.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7dee9b6b4fa01e7b310d973887043bfe</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Oscillatory Phenomena">
  <data key="d0">Oscillatory Phenomena</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Oscillatory Phenomena refer to the behavior of systems that exhibit periodic fluctuations, often seen in underdamped responses.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7dee9b6b4fa01e7b310d973887043bfe</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Frequency Response">
  <data key="d0">Frequency Response</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Frequency Response is a fundamental characteristic of systems, particularly in control systems and signal processing, that describes how a system reacts to different frequencies of input signals. It is crucial for analyzing and understanding system dynamics, stability, and performance. This response is typically characterized by changes in the magnitude and phase of the system's output as the input frequency varies. Frequency Response is often visualized using graphical representations such as Bode diagrams, Nyquist plots, and polar plots, which illustrate resonance peaks, phase shifts, and other key aspects of system behavior. These analyses help in designing and assessing the performance of systems by highlighting desirable and undesirable characteristics. The Frequency Response is essential for control system analysis and design, providing insights into the steady-state response of a system to sinusoidal inputs and serving as a quantitative measure of the output spectrum in response to a stimulus.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9f0dfc9266a7cbf0daf9292867c654cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a8c47160042a9398aa709e25eded3b0c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-181fee5061e5d9adf0f04d196cc15e7f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8a3a4cd5f5a625120a672d9302619e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d46c03f5b1a1f1ab07036c79e47616c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-62181afdae55ce4e95ff620bfa6e1818&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1022a5cf276c07ee56ffc50c13799b6d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f074d90ecc0d7974d2a0b0c59285149&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-550487a7cadc4b8eeb83211703d232ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e943fefbd15dc3bfc97bcb9515cd1eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-484e9407831fd22fae06241d1b7e75e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7dee9b6b4fa01e7b310d973887043bfe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cba4dc46aaf3979ba1619c43d08d1720&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-15b91f5c5b4a075330ef41ad3ec74fe9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7bfba099219ef0865c8cfbb638e366f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e0c2c5d2084cf4dc42eac20165445910&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ccb516dd7fa038fc65484f2cc9669722&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff7353abf978480820979c540d814ee3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fbfe186ba42a9341b463befd113d8ee4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a104cc76c4ded119be1e066101146986&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f7f4ddee3ffc4ad47062df678fff024&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-289220cc5e6fcc41f8da8923ec0e0105&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8baf5807e5435582388b6ba8ea165e4d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b0fa6b31797f4f5fd2bb265e6ef2851&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60969709c0f545814b039c0d77d040ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-855fbfd6cc8ae599aa41c969d6418c33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5ccf7d143be8a45626048d565c73daab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f59f8623e4ff8e64d49175daeeadad05&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b30d3f27196cdc41b81a736db5f1aee7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7617e3bbfe2c63a69317713315650eb3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98b7da91ec0504b2cb24aec37c61430a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc203beda6b14fd1cf52a94919ab90a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92e23c313eaf5a6d348bce8a1588be0f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e830557547fd0c9d37cbd07da38c0e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5ce576a87f38c3c3621dc3b3d8f16913&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b139b34ebbeaf26c5893fedc131b125&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d35fea10973c2b24ef34a97da4f0e8b</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
