<node id="Unit-Step Response Curve">
  <data key="d0">Unit-Step Response Curve</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The Unit-Step Response Curve is a graphical representation that illustrates the response of a system over time when subjected to a unit step input. It displays various dynamic characteristics of the system, such as overshoot, rise time, and settling time. The curve typically shows a rapid initial increase in amplitude followed by a slower rise, effectively capturing the system's behavior and amplitude changes in response to the step input. It serves as an essential tool for analyzing the performance of control systems with a given transfer function.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-91a2a152c44c8f2298858dd4c49a71a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9067de99754a18f08e6cfd3a76b28877&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4aecdf0555d89c0ebec0aa1b1b9980a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a3189f7cb3fb2865b828460dc211a36&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a6b4ef5ac67266af313e88e17c7523bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2bf2afdc6808412e18506f82583774c6</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
