<node id="Undamped Natural Frequency">
  <data key="d0">Undamped Natural Frequency</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The Undamped Natural Frequency is a fundamental characteristic of a system that describes the rate at which it oscillates in the absence of damping effects. It is the frequency at which a system would naturally oscillate if there were no damping present, often utilized in control system design to understand the system's oscillatory behavior. In the context of control systems, the undamped natural frequency is associated with the dominant closed-loop poles, indicating the speed of the transient response. It can be set to specific values, such as 2 rad/sec, to influence the system's oscillatory behavior. Additionally, in the analysis of a closed-loop system's unit-step response, the undamped natural frequency may be normalized to 1 for simplification. Overall, the undamped natural frequency is crucial in determining how quickly a system responds to changes without the influence of damping.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-36e714a094e63aef48fac634eeddad6c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da505be49d4d9c37eb80545921311479&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91a2a152c44c8f2298858dd4c49a71a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59498f3e851cf3c70c4395e945e7e809&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb2cafb27b000379bc871ea7923a83dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2281e4b3e341841f3ab4fc1ff9c7a634&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76155cfacd298ba99866d06587bc0e7d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a19f7091cfb7ee780a1c0268e833e55f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd970bcee6ec8782e0e15281c48fc6f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f571134d683a0689226e17f5c8f12d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ef9a9b21f3821e990c650615c128744&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9571f0c498fec38011c9f30cf7ab85ab</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
