<node id="Overshoot">
  <data key="d0">Overshoot</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Overshoot is a measure of the extent to which a system's output exceeds its target or final steady-state value during its transient response. It is commonly expressed as a percentage, indicating how much the system surpasses its intended target before stabilizing, with one example measurement being approximately 25%. This concept is crucial in understanding the behavior of control systems and their ability to reach desired performance levels.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7fb2f374d1a1fada7677f9980d7c9fe7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7cb24308be90f4de9c5775f0a3a25ce9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a59bbd3f86b4923fd22b10788ad73d53&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d0329f094fac40719bb16c44f090e26&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa017cb19dfa7211c0c2b6a589a80f57&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2bf2afdc6808412e18506f82583774c6</data>
