<node id="System Dynamics">
  <data key="d0">System Dynamics</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">System Dynamics refers to the mathematical modeling and analysis of the behavior of complex systems over time. It involves understanding how a system's behavior and performance respond to different input types, which can be analyzed through various graphs. The dynamics of a system are determined by the mathematical description provided by its state equations, involving matrices A and B, as well as by the placement of its closed-loop poles and feedback gain matrix. Additionally, system dynamics can be described by a transfer function with specific poles and coefficients, which together define the behavior of the system over time.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dfe09b7b703c389e8f2522a6967742f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5f8bc3750c711a5de6e8037c4fda4c0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fe015f4be9f2111ba91f577393b86cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1779b26d10c1b1abb7d91ca4e5524e77&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c1c7e149cb37d4947fe26456e62a591&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6daa8560d2825569846748debe43a15</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Exponential Input">
  <data key="d0">Exponential Input</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Exponential Input is a type of input signal that decreases exponentially over time, represented as e^{-t}.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5fe015f4be9f2111ba91f577393b86cd</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Response Curves">
  <data key="d0">Response Curves</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Response Curves are graphical representations that illustrate how a system's output reacts over time to specific input signals and initial conditions. These curves provide insights into the system's behavior by showing the oscillations and periodic behavior of variables such as x1, x2, and x3 over time. By graphically plotting the system's response to initial conditions, Response Curves help in understanding how state variables change over time, offering a comprehensive view of the system's dynamic behavior, as depicted in figures like Figure 10-21 and Figure 10-53.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0ea98dac7f834a445156f9d25aec3156&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-618424e4625f7d33fa3ab142d292d0b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fe015f4be9f2111ba91f577393b86cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ad73b7beb45180631dd72fbab2b6c9b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b31537ba5725a3819547235d3a68c08e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-670bc9d19f233014556f6058e19da1a2</data>
