<node id="Initial Condition">
  <data key="d0">Initial Condition</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Initial Condition refers to the starting state or values of a system, which significantly influence its subsequent behavior, response, and motion. In the context of simulations, such as those run in MATLAB, the initial condition is set to [1;0;1;0;t] and serves as a starting point or input parameter to analyze and generate response curves. These initial conditions are crucial for solving differential equations and determining the system's response, including aspects like initial displacement and velocity, which are predefined states impacting the mechanical system's subsequent behavior.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e6ca112b8faa4912569729a8f7b8746c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-284988f822bbc861f6935dafb7bde2c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ef015ac7f47a0b38f89f2063e63c2e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d179610b2c623234f00bb642b238054&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae9d94f8cb3004790ff22f37200c200d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7ee96b6c7a32a3b2a58081228221eda&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fe015f4be9f2111ba91f577393b86cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b31537ba5725a3819547235d3a68c08e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7b84f68967e01f789185103a6da424fa</data>
