  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Response to Initial Condition describes the behavior of a system over time as illustrated by a graph showing oscillations and damping effects.&lt;SEP&gt;Response to Initial Condition is the event depicted by the graph, showing how state variables x1 and x2 change over time in response to initial conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;The 'Response to Initial Condition' refers to the phenomenon being analyzed through graphs and equations in the text.&lt;SEP&gt;The response to initial condition refers to how a system behaves when it is subjected to an initial state or input.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b79361c4f9b3077dd7e1175a33749008&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d179610b2c623234f00bb642b238054&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-923b909910f72564cfae409c3c852e81&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b1f2a2888a1a638818b4914974061ec2</data>
