<node id="System Response">
  <data key="d0">System Response</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">System Response refers to the behavior and output of a system over time when subjected to initial conditions or various inputs. It is often analyzed using mathematical equations, matrices, and vectors, and can be depicted through graphs. The system's reaction is influenced by factors such as the placement of poles and gain matrices. System Response can involve different types of inputs, including step, ramp, and acceleration, and may be analyzed using tools such as MATLAB Program 10-32. It encompasses the behavior of mechanical systems when subjected to initial conditions and external forces, as well as control inputs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e6ca112b8faa4912569729a8f7b8746c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-332d7d5b6322874bc053c36563dd2b71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8051d18cbff63321d1754c1c1f43cd85&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ef015ac7f47a0b38f89f2063e63c2e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2edc55c9b1b51ced8a770b4a9cb7d0e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b495866d3d765a6bd3da8989d4656fc9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d2f61e38a659adbd5279f14d8bc0af8f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-670bc9d19f233014556f6058e19da1a2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7b84f68967e01f789185103a6da424fa</data>
