</node>
<node id="Equivalent Moment of Inertia">
  <data key="d0">Equivalent Moment of Inertia</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Equivalent Moment of Inertia is a measure used in dynamics to simplify the analysis of rotational systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Equivalent Moment of Inertia refers to the combined effect of moments of inertia in the gear train system.&lt;SEP&gt;The Equivalent Moment of Inertia, denoted as J1eq, is a parameter in the control system that influences the dynamic behavior of the system.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-faf6d229bd33d9a677ddb2c4f3fe8552&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4032b50ce14c0c3568bdbf73522823e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f220f834d3bf211bf1917f262c17e60d</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Control System Diagram">
  <data key="d0">Control System Diagram</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">A Control System Diagram is a schematic representation of a control system, showing components and their interactions.&lt;SEP&gt;A control system diagram is a graphical representation showing how different components interact within a system to achieve a desired outcome.&lt;SEP&gt;The Control System Diagram is a visual representation used in engineering and physics to illustrate the components and interactions within a control system.&lt;SEP&gt;The Control System Diagram visually represents the dynamics of a control system, showing elements like the transfer function, input signal, and feedback loop.&lt;SEP&gt;The control system diagram visually represents the components and interactions within a control system, including inputs, outputs, and feedback paths.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7fb6f6f4567355162f36e936387a3dc4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a7067d3378c6320f2be99583ea919091&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8b50aac79f087fdc5dd68834ab09cb3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb6a1e10709bc450dad65923e1301042&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f220f834d3bf211bf1917f262c17e60d</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Figure 5–52">
  <data key="d0">Figure 5–52</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Figure 5–52 refers to the specific illustration in the text showing the control system diagram and its unit-step response curve.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f220f834d3bf211bf1917f262c17e60d</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="J">
  <data key="d0">J</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">J represents the moment of inertia in the equations related to the control system dynamics.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f220f834d3bf211bf1917f262c17e60d</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="T">
  <data key="d0">T</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">T is a time-related parameter in the control system equations, affecting the system's dynamic behavior.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f220f834d3bf211bf1917f262c17e60d</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Gear Ratios">
  <data key="d0">Gear Ratios</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Gear Ratios, represented as N1/N2 and N3/N4, are used to calculate the effect on the equivalent moment of inertia and viscous-friction coefficient.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f220f834d3bf211bf1917f262c17e60d</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Response Curve">
  <data key="d0">Response Curve</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The Response Curve is a graphical representation of the system's output behavior over time following a unit-step input.&lt;SEP&gt;The response curve shows how the output signal changes in response to the input unit step disturbance, indicating system dynamics.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-692c80987f518b576a9461026d5a6aad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f220f834d3bf211bf1917f262c17e60d</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Dynamic Behavior">
  <data key="d0">Dynamic Behavior</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Dynamic Behavior refers to the system's response characteristics, including overshoot, settling time, and steady-state.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f220f834d3bf211bf1917f262c17e60d</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Controller Gain K">
  <data key="d0">Controller Gain K</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">K is the controller gain, a parameter that influences the system's response in the control system.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bde48fe7be57bee4bb18f23aaf9bf6a0</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
