<node id="Routh Array">
  <data key="d0">Routh Array</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Routh Array is a structured array used in the Routh Stability Criterion to evaluate the stability of a system based on its first column elements.&lt;SEP&gt;The Routh Array is a method used in control theory to determine the stability of a system by arranging the coefficients of a polynomial equation.&lt;SEP&gt;The Routh array is a tabular method used in control theory to determine the stability of a system based on its characteristic equation.&lt;SEP&gt;The Routh array is a tabular method used to determine the stability of a polynomial equation by organizing the coefficients in a specific format.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d45a98216ff7bfab744fda1466e1f2b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59252f7260535877b27b152342d1fa5d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c5e4f7e43e12b75521c4c048c3b222a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85b819ddf3cb3d7c56ca7d6f41195981</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
