</node>
<node id="Complex Open-loop Poles">
  <data key="d0">Complex Open-loop Poles</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Complex open-loop poles are mathematical points in control theory that require the determination of the angle of departure to understand root locus behavior.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ad53164b58b57cd02287907a08cfbb42</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Break-in Point">
  <data key="d0">Break-in Point</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">A break-in point is a location on the root locus where the path of the locus moves towards the real axis or a zero.&lt;SEP&gt;A break-in point is where root-locus branches coalesce as gain K is increased, indicating changes in system stability.&lt;SEP&gt;Break-in Point is a concept in control systems where branches of the root locus enter the real axis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-faf6d229bd33d9a677ddb2c4f3fe8552&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ad53164b58b57cd02287907a08cfbb42&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-586f97239ba09b5129d50fc14028adbc</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Angle of Departure">
  <data key="d0">Angle of Departure</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Angle of departure is the angle at which the root locus leaves a complex pole, calculated using vector summation from other poles and zeros.&lt;SEP&gt;Angle of departure is the angle at which the root locus leaves a complex pole, essential for analyzing system behavior in control theory.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ad53164b58b57cd02287907a08cfbb42&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53900274f2c35aaf0d99d0a9ee95f307</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
