<node id="Root Locus Plot">
  <data key="d0">Root Locus Plot</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The Root Locus Plot is a graphical representation used in control systems to analyze and design the system's stability and performance. It visualizes the movement of closed-loop poles as system parameters, particularly the gain parameter K, change. This tool is essential for understanding how the poles of a system evolve in response to varying gains, providing insights into the behavior of the system's poles and thereby aiding in the assessment of system stability and performance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c90833eb9af9b9addb524390cd11c1e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d98502cd8b9198221f2d4fb5c72719c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c51a48b42789ee6452aabf9684ca8e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb2cafb27b000379bc871ea7923a83dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c7d9a35f388915f791a96d8cdc32529b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8bb8d79a4bce9c3a0571e1ec2592d1a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3cea608f188f57be123ae911827b07d4</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Positive Feedback">
  <data key="d0">Positive Feedback</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Positive feedback is a type of feedback that can lead to instability in control systems, often requiring careful design considerations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8230d3f2f6d179c68a787d4d88412e94</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Input (R(s))">
  <data key="d0">Input (R(s))</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">R(s) is the input signal to the control system, which is processed to produce the desired output.&lt;SEP&gt;Represents the reference input or setpoint of the system in the block diagram.&lt;SEP&gt;The Input (R(s)) block represents the input signal to the control system.&lt;SEP&gt;The Input, denoted by R(s), represents the starting point of the control process in the system.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a5b3fa9ac1d3ce61d8dbdd21acb60d10&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ccfe5606d87942d95cd99b0924a1abcd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-35afe3e90a1acbe01560dbd9ac0de547&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3054b048b0a72e379da574dd802acf5c</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Output (C(s))">
  <data key="d0">Output (C(s))</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">C(s) is the output signal of the control system, representing the system's response to the input.&lt;SEP&gt;The Output (C(s)) block represents the output signal of the control system.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ccfe5606d87942d95cd99b0924a1abcd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-35afe3e90a1acbe01560dbd9ac0de547</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Break-in Points">
  <data key="d0">Break-in Points</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Break-in points are locations on the root locus where branches of the locus converge onto the real axis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8d688cebd148c9433a92b32b02bb240b</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="K (Gain)">
  <data key="d0">K (Gain)</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">K is the gain factor in the characteristic equation, affecting the position and shape of the root locus.&lt;SEP&gt;K represents the gain in a control system, affecting the stability and performance of the system.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-586f97239ba09b5129d50fc14028adbc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8d688cebd148c9433a92b32b02bb240b</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Complex Pole">
  <data key="d0">Complex Pole</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Complex Pole refers to a point in the s-plane used in control systems to analyze system stability and performance.&lt;SEP&gt;Complex poles are poles with both real and imaginary components, specifically at s=-1+j and s=-1-j.&lt;SEP&gt;Complex poles are poles with imaginary components, influencing system dynamics and transient response.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a5f65ec7a6f616b6865aa6c974202119&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53900274f2c35aaf0d99d0a9ee95f307&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfaabf07740c618e0c89f07d1cf48dea</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Complex Zero">
  <data key="d0">Complex Zero</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Complex Zero is a point in the s-plane similar to poles, used to determine system behavior in control theory.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bfaabf07740c618e0c89f07d1cf48dea</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="S-plane">
  <data key="d0">S-plane</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The S-plane is a complex plane used in control theory to plot poles and zeros of a system for stability analysis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bfaabf07740c618e0c89f07d1cf48dea</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
