<node id="Root-Locus Plot">
  <data key="d0">Root-Locus Plot</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The Root-Locus Plot is a graphical representation used extensively in control systems engineering to analyze and design system stability and performance. It illustrates the potential locations and trajectories of the poles of a system's characteristic equation or transfer function in the complex plane as a specific system parameter, typically gain, varies. By showing how the roots of a polynomial or the system's poles and zeros change with varying parameters, the Root-Locus Plot provides critical insights into the system's stability, behavior, and response characteristics. This tool is instrumental in determining system stability, analyzing pole placement, and understanding the effects of poles and zeros on system performance. Through its graphical depiction, the Root-Locus Plot aids engineers in examining changes in a control system's poles and zeros, thereby facilitating the design and analysis of control systems.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-45d58fa0ad7e2ced2585b4512c2f59e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7fb2f374d1a1fada7677f9980d7c9fe7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-36e714a094e63aef48fac634eeddad6c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7124a0bbfe59c091664e7c98717fbde3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37550db7b78b6550ac3a1bbeaf90fe63&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-12f9482a2de5a4049338d2f20af641c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd970bcee6ec8782e0e15281c48fc6f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a8712fa7ddd9dc034d222eaf660d62f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e3282077e1fe73808ab0efe43eaa3b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-47472143ed7851235eb43e5eb130bc1c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-526791d98cb78b5ccbbec0c10ad8ce82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec1fe4f707d8920dbeac015fecfd158e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db115ced573d3098e7cb02b4ddf8625f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-61e97a29a080915ebe1313dbe1f7440e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7fb6f6f4567355162f36e936387a3dc4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5d9384ff4d2caf674fcfb9545ee0e6b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc4f091219e1ee158ce8e0f022f44c42&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0690050aa436f47134092f69ec8ed18b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf299ff5c8d29fc06d76cf7459e022b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c7a1931ad2ca3ae471cd3b57aa9a81eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88ad04f5c92febfb736b3e73f1b155d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-610f25557b703d8c29a8efc2d292eb77&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d30d89b485b27ebd673bf1d2c57c24a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-486351ecd11a42798affd79b7f5d143b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51ed07bf7b1b56e1246deb3b4a2fd5cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-441dbc13e7ef7807ed52d100c9a4f041&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59a053a060eb4f14d77b34ae1061cace&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4401dd3428e0cf00f995665a23c44646&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-862057e40203dab14f5b486a9fcc1a5a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92e23c313eaf5a6d348bce8a1588be0f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37c3fea424ed4692d82113ae9fd3f941&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-feb8129fd0acf4bdee571b9fbeafe347&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b52720f9a7352e99f41bd87710c52e0f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8fb07569a4fb35322f960ef1bd2a2a89&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e83e0b0f093a4a5ee928c26cb73ad75</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Complex-Conjugate Open-Loop Poles">
  <data key="d0">Complex-Conjugate Open-Loop Poles</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Complex-conjugate open-loop poles are the roots of the polynomial equation s^2 + 4s + 16 = 0, which are critical for determining system stability.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8fb07569a4fb35322f960ef1bd2a2a89</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
