<node id="Denominator Polynomial">
  <data key="d0">Denominator Polynomial</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The denominator polynomial is a product of first- and second-order terms, represented as [1, 5, 20, 16, 0] in the system equation.&lt;SEP&gt;The denominator polynomial is part of the transfer function, representing the system's dynamics.&lt;SEP&gt;The denominator polynomial represents the denominator of a transfer function in the frequency domain.&lt;SEP&gt;The polynomial representing the denominator of the transfer function in the root-locus plot, defined by coefficients [1, 4, 6, 4, 1].</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4401dd3428e0cf00f995665a23c44646&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-016ebe44f8f410b4e420081ccf7a65f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8fb07569a4fb35322f960ef1bd2a2a89&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-86ce58db4d75e50b5241f0be0e62c4c5</data>
