<node id="Root-Locus Diagram">
  <data key="d0">Root-Locus Diagram</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The Root-Locus Diagram is a graphical representation used in control systems and control theory to analyze the effects of varying system parameters on the locations of closed-loop poles. It serves as a diagram for illustrating both open-loop poles and desired closed-loop poles. This plot is particularly useful for showing the paths of the poles of a transfer function as system parameters are varied, thus allowing for the examination of how the roots of a control system change. Additionally, the Root-Locus Diagram is employed to analyze the stability of complex systems, providing valuable insights into the system's behavior under different conditions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f104d09d0c472d244729f4c0273b66e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5e2669ac54f338b1cf942ce034ed4ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37550db7b78b6550ac3a1bbeaf90fe63&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b55f24e9f9505c14159b689d1ef175f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b54450b954742096d3c9cc14431cc98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-962404cbdd61044ac178296d6d459eed</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
