<node id="Static Velocity Error Constant Kv">
  <data key="d0">Static Velocity Error Constant Kv</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">A parameter in control systems representing the steady-state error for velocity inputs, with a specified value of 80 sec^-1.&lt;SEP&gt;Kv is a constant that measures the steady-state error in velocity within a control system.&lt;SEP&gt;Kv is a measure of the system's steady-state error in response to a velocity input, calculated from the system's transfer function.&lt;SEP&gt;Static velocity error constant Kv is a measure of a system's ability to track a ramp input.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0a41b322606e11a7a7d3758a0cae0e29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb6a1e10709bc450dad65923e1301042&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b52720f9a7352e99f41bd87710c52e0f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d2c20fec382eb167929db2080ec8c24</data>
