<node id="Origin">
  <data key="d0">Origin</data>
  <data key="d1">geo</data>
  <data key="d2">The Origin is a point in the coordinate system, often used as a reference point in mathematical diagrams.&lt;SEP&gt;The origin is the central point on a graph, marked by zero, serving as a reference for plotting complex numbers.&lt;SEP&gt;The origin is the point (0, 0) where the real and imaginary axes intersect on the complex number plane.&lt;SEP&gt;The origin is the point where the real and imaginary axes intersect, marked as (0,0) in the complex number plane.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-61e97a29a080915ebe1313dbe1f7440e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-814b833e231cf6e96b1f333e7eb5bbc4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b52720f9a7352e99f41bd87710c52e0f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9afe985fc7dab84bc86b6f660723b27e</data>
