  <data key="d2">Root-Locus Plots are graphical representations used to analyze the roots of a system as a parameter, such as gain, is varied.&lt;SEP&gt;Root-locus plots are graphical representations that show the trajectories of system poles in the complex plane as a parameter varies, used to analyze system stability and performance.</data>
