  <data key="d2">Kv is the static velocity error constant specified in the control system design, indicating the steady-state error in velocity response.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7f571134d683a0689226e17f5c8f12d2</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Kc">
  <data key="d0">Kc</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">A variable representing the gain of the compensator in the mathematical equation.&lt;SEP&gt;Kc is a constant used in the control system, related to the compensator's gain and affecting system performance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-51ed07bf7b1b56e1246deb3b4a2fd5cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f571134d683a0689226e17f5c8f12d2</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="T1">
  <data key="d0">T1</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">A variable in the equation, possibly representing a time constant or parameter in the control system.&lt;SEP&gt;T1 is a time constant in the lag-lead compensator, affecting the system's phase and magnitude response.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-51ed07bf7b1b56e1246deb3b4a2fd5cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f571134d683a0689226e17f5c8f12d2</data>
