  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Trial-and-error calculations are iterative methods used to find suitable values for unknowns in equations, applied here to solve for beta and x.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8f1f8bc5cab7c0486a4991400b504ed8</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Attitude-Rate Control System">
  <data key="d0">Attitude-Rate Control System</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The attitude-rate control system is a model used to control the orientation rate of an object, often represented in block diagrams.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-61e97a29a080915ebe1313dbe1f7440e</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Aircraft">
  <data key="d0">Aircraft</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The aircraft is the main system being controlled by the autopilot system, responding to control inputs to maintain altitude.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f1e2f536a2499c393f143367bb8b5da9</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Hydraulic Servo">
  <data key="d0">Hydraulic Servo</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The Hydraulic Servo is a component that controls the aircraft's pitch and yaw movements, represented by the transfer function Gc(s) = 1/s.&lt;SEP&gt;The hydraulic servo converts electrical signals into hydraulic pressure to actuate the aircraft's elevator or rudder.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fef16edcd77ce0c9e06d5d42a6b361da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1e2f536a2499c393f143367bb8b5da9</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Rate Gyro">
  <data key="d0">Rate Gyro</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">A rate gyro is a rate feedback device commonly used in aircraft autopilot systems.&lt;SEP&gt;The Rate Gyro is a device used in control systems to measure angular velocity, providing input signals for state equations.&lt;SEP&gt;The Rate Gyro measures angular velocity of the aircraft around its pitch and yaw axes, represented by the transfer function Gry(s) = 1/s.&lt;SEP&gt;The rate gyro measures the angular rate of rotation about a specific axis and provides feedback to the control system.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fef16edcd77ce0c9e06d5d42a6b361da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d424f9b5c8e1c4caa0b22f889469da1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69b1697f44d2725bfd2f580c242ea9b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1e2f536a2499c393f143367bb8b5da9</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Compensator Design">
  <data key="d0">Compensator Design</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Compensator design refers to the process of designing a control mechanism to improve system response and eliminate oscillations.&lt;SEP&gt;The process of designing a compensator to achieve specific performance criteria, such as maximum overshoot and settling time.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f1e2f536a2499c393f143367bb8b5da9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8639c1dbc2042e150feddfc5fe82ffe8</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
