<node id="Aircraft Dynamics">
  <data key="d0">Aircraft Dynamics</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Aircraft Dynamics models the dynamics of the aircraft, including mass, inertia, and damping, represented by the transfer function 1/s^2.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fef16edcd77ce0c9e06d5d42a6b361da</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Control Loop">
  <data key="d0">Control Loop</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The Control Loop involves a PID controller that adjusts the hydraulic servo's output to stabilize the aircraft's attitude, featuring proportional, integral, and derivative gains.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fef16edcd77ce0c9e06d5d42a6b361da</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Compensated Attitude-Rate Control System">
  <data key="d0">Compensated Attitude-Rate Control System</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">A system designed to stabilize aircraft attitude by adjusting control inputs based on feedback.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fef16edcd77ce0c9e06d5d42a6b361da</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Proportional-Integral-Derivative (PID) Controller">
  <data key="d0">Proportional-Integral-Derivative (PID) Controller</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">A control mechanism in the control loop that uses proportional, integral, and derivative gains to stabilize the aircraft.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fef16edcd77ce0c9e06d5d42a6b361da</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Compensator $G_{c}(s)$">
  <data key="d0">Compensator $G_{c}(s)$</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The Compensator $G_{c}(s)$ is a mathematical function added to the system to modify its dynamic behavior, aiming to improve stability and performance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-feb8129fd0acf4bdee571b9fbeafe347</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Complex Numbers">
  <data key="d0">Complex Numbers</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Complex Numbers are mathematical entities expressed in the form z = x + yi or a + bi, where x and a represent the real part, and y and b represent the imaginary part. These numbers have both real and imaginary components and are used extensively in a variety of fields, including electrical engineering, physics, and advanced mathematical computations. Complex numbers are crucial in mathematical representations, calculations, and functions, and they are often depicted graphically in both rectangular and polar forms, such as in diagrams and polar plots. Their applications are diverse, spanning mathematical and engineering contexts, where they play a significant role in equations and graphical representations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-094d0f53918a4b57661980c588c5dd88&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb053307052f18015012648da15e3c35&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9afe985fc7dab84bc86b6f660723b27e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-814b833e231cf6e96b1f333e7eb5bbc4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2160cb6aaf30b68e3cbc695bfa7548cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-83bded94a3ff142ba41772e1b37f4f63&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd5a5410abc287fd3f4c9718236dc051&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-feb8129fd0acf4bdee571b9fbeafe347&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d35fea10973c2b24ef34a97da4f0e8b</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
