</node>
<node id="Velocity Feedback Gain k">
  <data key="d0">Velocity Feedback Gain k</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Velocity Feedback Gain k is a parameter that influences the damping and stability of a control system.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7fb6f6f4567355162f36e936387a3dc4</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Velocity Feedback Gain">
  <data key="d0">Velocity Feedback Gain</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Velocity feedback gain refers to the proportional gain in a control system that affects the velocity response of the system.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0b429aa524429e2d3a0bb88587574c34</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Complex Poles">
  <data key="d0">Complex Poles</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Complex poles are poles of a transfer function that have both real and imaginary parts, affecting the stability and response of a control system.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0b429aa524429e2d3a0bb88587574c34</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Equation of a Circle">
  <data key="d0">Equation of a Circle</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">An equation representing a circle with a specific center and radius, used in geometric and frequency response analysis.&lt;SEP&gt;The equation of a circle is a mathematical representation of a circle's geometry, used here to describe the root locus.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2f7f4ddee3ffc4ad47062df678fff024&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b429aa524429e2d3a0bb88587574c34</data>
