  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Magnitude Response is a plot showing the system's gain at different frequencies, indicating resonant frequencies and peak gains.&lt;SEP&gt;Magnitude Response refers to the graphical representation of a system's output, measured in dB, plotted against angular frequency (rad/sec).&lt;SEP&gt;Magnitude response indicates how the amplitude of a system's output varies with frequency, often shown in decibels.&lt;SEP&gt;Magnitude response is a part of the Bode diagram, representing the system's gain in decibels across frequencies.&lt;SEP&gt;The Magnitude Response is part of the Bode diagram, depicted in decibels, showing the system's reaction to frequency changes.</data>
