<node id="Unit Circle">
  <data key="d0">Unit Circle</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The Unit Circle is a circle in the complex plane with a radius of one, used in Nyquist plots to determine system stability.&lt;SEP&gt;The unit circle is a circle with a radius of 1, centered at the origin in the Cartesian coordinate system, used in trigonometry to define sine and cosine functions.&lt;SEP&gt;Unit Circle is a circle with a radius of one, used in Nyquist plots to indicate stability margins and phase relationships.&lt;SEP&gt;Unit Circle serves as a reference in a Nyquist plot, representing the frequency response of a system at unity gain.</data>
