  <data key="d0">Log-Magnitude-Versus-Phase Plot</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">A log-magnitude-versus-phase plot, also known as a Nichols plot, combines logarithmic magnitude and phase angle to depict frequency response characteristics.&lt;SEP&gt;Log-magnitude-versus-phase plot shows relationship between magnitude and phase of a transfer function.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2afbc3d7bb9c389990910a284d3b9dfd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1022a5cf276c07ee56ffc50c13799b6d</data>
