<node id="G(s)H(s)">
  <data key="d0">G(s)H(s)</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">G(s)H(s) is a mathematical function representing a product of transfer functions, analyzed in the context of complex functions.&lt;SEP&gt;G(s)H(s) is the open-loop transfer function in control systems, typically expressed as the ratio of two polynomials in s, which is analyzed for stability using the Nyquist Criterion.&lt;SEP&gt;G(s)H(s) is the open-loop transfer function of a control system, used in stability analysis.&lt;SEP&gt;G(s)H(s) represents the open-loop transfer function of a system, which is analyzed for stability through Nyquist plots and other methods.&lt;SEP&gt;The open-loop transfer function of a control system, used to determine system behavior and stability.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b780aae2274d6d12811004661f2bb425&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-021d406fb1875a04e6ca85d6a4589897&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-814b833e231cf6e96b1f333e7eb5bbc4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1fc8172454011b7e111636e450b0431d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d08ffa0936970988485d30a9ea44afb</data>
