  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The Argument Principle is a concept in complex analysis that relates the integral of a function over a closed curve to its poles inside the curve.&lt;SEP&gt;The argument principle is a technique in complex analysis used to count zeros and poles of an analytic function within a contour in the complex plane.</data>
