  <data key="d0">Complex-Conjugate Closed-Loop Poles</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">These poles dominate the frequency response of higher-order systems, allowing for correlation with standard second-order systems.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3b0fa6b31797f4f5fd2bb265e6ef2851</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Resonant Frequency (\omega_{r})">
  <data key="d0">Resonant Frequency (\omega_{r})</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The resonant frequency is indicative of the system's speed of transient response and influences the rise time.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3b0fa6b31797f4f5fd2bb265e6ef2851</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Resonant Peak (M_{r})">
  <data key="d0">Resonant Peak (M_{r})</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The resonant peak measures the relative stability of a system and affects transient overshoot behavior.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3b0fa6b31797f4f5fd2bb265e6ef2851</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Damping Ratio (\zeta)">
  <data key="d0">Damping Ratio (\zeta)</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The damping ratio affects the system's transient response, influencing overshoot and rise time.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3b0fa6b31797f4f5fd2bb265e6ef2851</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Bandwidth">
  <data key="d0">Bandwidth</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Bandwidth in control systems refers to the range of frequencies over which a system can operate effectively. This range is crucial as it determines the system's ability to respond without significant signal attenuation and is inversely related to rise time, influencing the speed of response. Bandwidth is often measured in radians per second, with a specific example being approximately 3.8 rad/sec for System 2. It is defined as the frequency range within which the system response is above a specified magnitude threshold, and it plays a significant role in the transmission of signals within a given band.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-92e23c313eaf5a6d348bce8a1588be0f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1df4ff44b7c85b353430b33b36adb1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27923b259bf2de83650da5b28f76726e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b0fa6b31797f4f5fd2bb265e6ef2851&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-189305ffdfb5a3f7a9695e56559bcef3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60969709c0f545814b039c0d77d040ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e2d5c8521bc1f35d5a5daaf0b7fe7eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-471b11b0e8da61744401ac854b4948f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5ab66ab2ea102011daec41a066d3877c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e83e0b0f093a4a5ee928c26cb73ad75</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Cutoff Frequency (\omega_{b})">
  <data key="d0">Cutoff Frequency (\omega_{b})</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The cutoff frequency defines the point where the closed-loop frequency response falls below a specified level.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3b0fa6b31797f4f5fd2bb265e6ef2851</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Closed-loop Frequency Response">
  <data key="d0">Closed-loop Frequency Response</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Closed-loop Frequency Response refers to the behavior of a system when feedback is applied, measured in terms of magnitude and phase angle at different frequency points.&lt;SEP&gt;Closed-loop frequency response describes how a system reacts to various frequencies, influencing stability and signal distinction.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-27923b259bf2de83650da5b28f76726e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f86521265de1eaaef568da798d2e3a53</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="System I">
  <data key="d0">System I</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">System I is characterized by a wider bandwidth, allowing faster response and better input tracking compared to System II.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-27923b259bf2de83650da5b28f76726e</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="System II">
  <data key="d0">System II</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">System II has a narrower bandwidth, resulting in slower response and less effective input tracking compared to System I.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-27923b259bf2de83650da5b28f76726e</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Noise Filtering">
  <data key="d0">Noise Filtering</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Noise filtering involves reducing unwanted high-frequency noise, which can conflict with the requirements for large bandwidth.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-27923b259bf2de83650da5b28f76726e</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Stability Margin">
  <data key="d0">Stability Margin</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Stability margin refers to the degree to which a system can withstand disturbances without losing stability.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-27923b259bf2de83650da5b28f76726e</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Resonant Frequency">
  <data key="d0">Resonant Frequency</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Resonant Frequency is the frequency at which the maximum magnitude occurs in a system's frequency response.&lt;SEP&gt;Resonant Frequency is the frequency at which the system exhibits the resonant peak value, critical for understanding system dynamics.&lt;SEP&gt;Resonant frequency is the frequency at which a system naturally oscillates with maximum amplitude, important for understanding system dynamics.&lt;SEP&gt;Resonant frequency is the frequency at which a system's magnitude response reaches its peak, indicating maximum energy storage.&lt;SEP&gt;The resonant frequency is the frequency at which a system's response is at its peak, indicating maximum energy transfer.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-96a98f812e32e184c15978c0d7771176&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-061cf1e0924989ccbea19f388762245a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-189305ffdfb5a3f7a9695e56559bcef3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60969709c0f545814b039c0d77d040ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e2d5c8521bc1f35d5a5daaf0b7fe7eb</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
