<node id="G(jω) Locus">
  <data key="d0">G(jω) Locus</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The G(jω) Locus is a plot of the open-loop frequency response, used to analyze system behavior in terms of gain and phase shift.&lt;SEP&gt;The G(jω) locus represents the open-loop frequency response and is used to find intersections with M and N circles.&lt;SEP&gt;The G(jω) locus represents the path traced by the open-loop transfer function in the frequency response analysis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2f7f4ddee3ffc4ad47062df678fff024&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-189305ffdfb5a3f7a9695e56559bcef3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-061cf1e0924989ccbea19f388762245a</data>
