<node id="Nichols Chart">
  <data key="d0">Nichols Chart</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The Nichols Chart is a graphical representation used in control system design to analyze gain and phase characteristics of closed-loop systems.&lt;SEP&gt;The Nichols Chart is a graphical tool used to represent the frequency response of a system, showing magnitude and phase angle.&lt;SEP&gt;The Nichols chart is a graphical representation used to analyze frequency response in control systems, showing relationships between magnitude and phase.&lt;SEP&gt;The Nichols chart is a graphical tool used in control engineering to assess system stability and performance.&lt;SEP&gt;The Nichols chart is a graphical tool used in control systems to display frequency response data, particularly useful for determining system gain and phase margins.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-061cf1e0924989ccbea19f388762245a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-189305ffdfb5a3f7a9695e56559bcef3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30758f9c11d60c2ad7dbc4a84ff615d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf4e759f85cb69aeac07e60c7ccbf414&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-62181afdae55ce4e95ff620bfa6e1818</data>
