<node id="Type 0 Systems">
  <data key="d0">Type 0 Systems</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Type 0 systems are characterized by a constant gain at low frequencies, represented by a horizontal asymptote in the log-magnitude curve.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7c16de2cbe7e947bb8bc1c1fd886e33c</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Type 1 Systems">
  <data key="d0">Type 1 Systems</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Type 1 systems have a gain that decreases with frequency, characterized by a -20 dB/decade slope in the log-magnitude curve.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7c16de2cbe7e947bb8bc1c1fd886e33c</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Type 2 Systems">
  <data key="d0">Type 2 Systems</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Type 2 systems have a gain that decreases more rapidly with frequency, characterized by a -40 dB/decade slope in the log-magnitude curve.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7c16de2cbe7e947bb8bc1c1fd886e33c</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Nonminimum-Phase Transfer Functions">
  <data key="d0">Nonminimum-Phase Transfer Functions</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Nonminimum-phase transfer functions are characterized by phase angles at high frequencies that differ from expected values, indicating the presence of transport lag or dead time.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-955b6d1a9437f260081a7c8bfe86f0af</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
