<node id="PD Controller">
  <data key="d0">PD Controller</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">A type of controller with a proportional and derivative component, represented by the transfer function Gc(s) = 5(1 + 0.5s).&lt;SEP&gt;PD Controller refers to a proportional-derivative controller used in control systems to improve stability and response.&lt;SEP&gt;The PD Controller is a simplified lead compensator used in control systems to meet steady-state requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;The PD controller is a simplified version of the lead compensator, acting as a high-pass filter and improving transient-response characteristics.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-15b91f5c5b4a075330ef41ad3ec74fe9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96901c8e0575c3c8488667c451ac4616&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c7a34174c65e8a6a1a11ac9ee67b0bbe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b495866d3d765a6bd3da8989d4656fc9</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="PI Controller">
  <data key="d0">PI Controller</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">A type of controller with a proportional and integral component, represented by the transfer function Gc(s) = 5(1 + 1/(2s)).&lt;SEP&gt;PI Controller refers to a proportional-integral controller used in control systems for enhanced accuracy and stability.&lt;SEP&gt;The PI Controller is a type of control system characterized by its transfer function, improving steady-state characteristics but potentially reducing system stability.&lt;SEP&gt;The PI controller is a type of control system that acts as a low-pass filter, attenuating high-frequency components of the signal.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-15b91f5c5b4a075330ef41ad3ec74fe9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96901c8e0575c3c8488667c451ac4616&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c7a34174c65e8a6a1a11ac9ee67b0bbe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b495866d3d765a6bd3da8989d4656fc9</data>
