<node id="Closed-loop Transfer Function">
  <data key="d0">Closed-loop Transfer Function</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">A closed-loop transfer function describes the relationship between the input and output of a system in a feedback loop.&lt;SEP&gt;A mathematical representation of a system's response with feedback, given by C(s)/R(s) = G(s)/(1 + G(s)).&lt;SEP&gt;The closed-loop transfer function describes the mathematical relationship between Y(s) and D(s) in the system.&lt;SEP&gt;The closed-loop transfer function represents the relationship between the input and output of a control system, highlighting system dynamics.&lt;SEP&gt;The mathematical representation of the system's response to inputs, considering the feedback loop and PID controller.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-35a3e069b7dbf5f1a07b6215423095e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d46c03f5b1a1f1ab07036c79e47616c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8fa18514b224d24d7347ad430cc2b575&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a954f327a9c49380980f7f1e64531f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97ff6cf0253e8f192c45acefe4824e0b</data>
