<node id="Ziegler-Nichols Method">
  <data key="d0">Ziegler-Nichols Method</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The Ziegler-Nichols Method is a set of rules for tuning PID controllers, involving specific formulas and procedures to set parameters for optimal system performance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6f67e9b469ce0543584be32ab4c6f89c</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Kp">
  <data key="d0">Kp</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Kp is the proportional gain in the PID controller, affecting system stability and performance.&lt;SEP&gt;Kp is the proportional gain parameter in a PID controller, affecting the speed of the system's response.&lt;SEP&gt;Kp, or the proportional gain, is a parameter of the PID controller affecting the control signal's response to the error signal.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bb690227c0aeb29078796de6d1611d85&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b55f24e9f9505c14159b689d1ef175f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f67e9b469ce0543584be32ab4c6f89c</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Ti">
  <data key="d0">Ti</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Ti is the integral time constant in a PID controller, determining the accumulation of past errors for corrective action.&lt;SEP&gt;Ti is the integral time constant in a PID controller, influencing how quickly the integral term reacts to accumulated errors.&lt;SEP&gt;Ti is the integral time constant in the PID controller, affecting the system's response to errors.&lt;SEP&gt;Ti is the integral time constant of a controller, determining the speed at which the integral term responds to changes in the error signal.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bb690227c0aeb29078796de6d1611d85&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b55f24e9f9505c14159b689d1ef175f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f87ef3fd6a4c1856d15e4ad169e98183&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f67e9b469ce0543584be32ab4c6f89c</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Td">
  <data key="d0">Td</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Td is the derivative time constant in a PID controller, determining the response to the rate of change of the error.&lt;SEP&gt;Td is the derivative time constant in a PID controller, predicting future error based on its rate of change.&lt;SEP&gt;Td is the derivative time constant in the PID controller, influencing the system's reaction to change.&lt;SEP&gt;Td is the derivative time constant of a controller, influencing the rate at which the derivative term reacts to changes in the error signal.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bb690227c0aeb29078796de6d1611d85&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b55f24e9f9505c14159b689d1ef175f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f87ef3fd6a4c1856d15e4ad169e98183&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f67e9b469ce0543584be32ab4c6f89c</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
