  <data key="d0">Output (c(t))</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Output, denoted as c(t), is the actual response of the system being controlled, measured to assess system performance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6f67e9b469ce0543584be32ab4c6f89c</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Critical Gain (Kcr)">
  <data key="d0">Critical Gain (Kcr)</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Critical Gain, denoted as Kcr, is the gain value at which a system first exhibits sustained oscillations, used in tuning control systems.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6f67e9b469ce0543584be32ab4c6f89c</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Critical Period (Pcr)">
  <data key="d0">Critical Period (Pcr)</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Critical Period, denoted as Pcr, is the period of oscillation when a system first exhibits sustained oscillations, important for control system tuning.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6f67e9b469ce0543584be32ab4c6f89c</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Ziegler–Nichols Tuning Rule">
  <data key="d0">Ziegler–Nichols Tuning Rule</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">A method used to determine the values of PID controller parameters to achieve desired system performance.&lt;SEP&gt;The Ziegler–Nichols tuning rule is a heuristic method for tuning PID controllers to achieve desired system responses.&lt;SEP&gt;The Ziegler–Nichols tuning rule is a heuristic method of tuning a PID controller to achieve optimal performance.&lt;SEP&gt;The Ziegler–Nichols tuning rule is a heuristic method of tuning a PID controller. It provides a starting point for tuning by setting certain parameters.&lt;SEP&gt;Ziegler–Nichols tuning rules are methods used for tuning PID controllers in control systems, especially when plant dynamics are not precisely known.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c90a28b31b0ff2333ffc79bc30b633af&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb690227c0aeb29078796de6d1611d85&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b55f24e9f9505c14159b689d1ef175f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0bfe9ed85a05514b41c868536d544660&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c90e64ef4d3ea69c9b12410204a70bfb</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
