<node id="System Stability">
  <data key="d0">System Stability</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">System Stability refers to the ability of a system to maintain its performance without oscillating or diverging.&lt;SEP&gt;System stability refers to the ability of a system to maintain its state or return to a desired state after disturbances.&lt;SEP&gt;The ability of a system to maintain its state or return to it after a disturbance.&lt;SEP&gt;The characteristic of the control system that ensures it remains functional and responsive to inputs, indicated by pole positions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-94456e2884706eeb42e67b6c40918a79&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a954f327a9c49380980f7f1e64531f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-289220cc5e6fcc41f8da8923ec0e0105&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ad1dc64fc9b2da439067495b6c1bf166</data>
