<node id="Sorting Algorithms">
  <data key="d0">Sorting Algorithms</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Sorting Algorithms refer to techniques for arranging data, including Bubble Sort, Selection Sort, Insertion Sort, Merge Sort, and Quick Sort.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-115c47567f4cb2d5b0df6b61937e6281</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="K Parameter">
  <data key="d0">K Parameter</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">K Parameter is a variable in the control system that affects rise time and maximum overshoot, crucial for system tuning.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-115c47567f4cb2d5b0df6b61937e6281</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="a Parameter">
  <data key="d0">a Parameter</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">a Parameter is a variable in the control system that influences system behavior, including settling time and overshoot.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-115c47567f4cb2d5b0df6b61937e6281</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Bubble Sort">
  <data key="d0">Bubble Sort</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Bubble Sort is a basic sorting algorithm known for its simplicity but poor performance on large datasets, where its execution time significantly increases.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7fe680e879a6164f9dd5b97f2340c3e2</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Merge Sort">
  <data key="d0">Merge Sort</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Merge Sort is an efficient, stable, and divide-and-conquer-based sorting algorithm that performs well on large datasets.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7fe680e879a6164f9dd5b97f2340c3e2</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Quick Sort">
  <data key="d0">Quick Sort</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Quick Sort is a highly efficient sorting algorithm that uses a divide-and-conquer approach and performs well with large datasets.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7fe680e879a6164f9dd5b97f2340c3e2</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
