<node id="Two-degrees-of-freedom control system">
  <data key="d0">Two-degrees-of-freedom control system</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">A control system design that allows for independent adjustment of two variables, enhancing flexibility and performance in signal processing.&lt;SEP&gt;A control system design that allows for separate handling of reference tracking and disturbance rejection.&lt;SEP&gt;A control system designed to manage input signals through various blocks, including filters and adders, to achieve desired output with specific performance criteria such as maximum overshoot and settling time.&lt;SEP&gt;The Two-degrees-of-freedom control system is a type of control system depicted in Figure 8–80.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7cb24308be90f4de9c5775f0a3a25ce9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-952ac88fc20d94741d460ff36bcefd2c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d4db33b4e6388556833f75db47703f2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-799625a96afba94ba9a1c4461a64170d</data>
