  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">An omit-step reference input is a type of input signal that demonstrates a rapid increase followed by a gradual decrease over time.&lt;SEP&gt;Omit-Step Reference Input refers to a type of input in a system response analysis, characterized by a rapid increase followed by a gradual decrease.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-aa017cb19dfa7211c0c2b6a589a80f57&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-692c80987f518b576a9461026d5a6aad</data>
