  <data key="d0">Example 9–2</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Example 9–2 demonstrates the state-space representation of a system using matrices A, B, and C.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5e25465698e9728fefd91973fb2caccd</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Transformation Matrix P">
  <data key="d0">Transformation Matrix P</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">A matrix used to transform another matrix into a diagonal form.&lt;SEP&gt;Transformation Matrix P is used to diagonalize Matrix A, transforming it into Diagonal Matrix D.&lt;SEP&gt;Transformation Matrix P is used to modify the coefficient matrix into a diagonal matrix, playing a critical role in the linear transformation process.&lt;SEP&gt;Transformation matrix P is used to diagonalize matrix A when its eigenvectors are distinct, simplifying analysis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-37b28f4da7cad971f45737e82572ff87&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e37fd32e67cfb4b06fcec5633146e195&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5f8bc3750c711a5de6e8037c4fda4c0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df340b9017a894bdcfdb18b9aa3427b6</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Coefficient Matrix">
  <data key="d0">Coefficient Matrix</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The Coefficient Matrix is transformed into a diagonal matrix by the Transformation Matrix P, indicating its role in matrix operations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-37b28f4da7cad971f45737e82572ff87</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Scalar State Equations">
  <data key="d0">Scalar State Equations</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Scalar State Equations are uncoupled equations derived from the diagonal matrix, illustrating the mathematical structure of the system.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-37b28f4da7cad971f45737e82572ff87</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Linear Transformation">
  <data key="d0">Linear Transformation</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Linear Transformation is a process that maintains the invariance of eigenvalues, as demonstrated by the transformation matrix P.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-37b28f4da7cad971f45737e82572ff87</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Characteristic Polynomials">
  <data key="d0">Characteristic Polynomials</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Characteristic Polynomials are used to prove the invariance of eigenvalues under linear transformations, highlighting the mathematical consistency.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-37b28f4da7cad971f45737e82572ff87</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
