</node>
<node id="Homogeneous State Equation">
  <data key="d0">Homogeneous State Equation</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Homogeneous State Equation refers to a type of differential equation where the function and its derivatives are proportional, often solved using matrix exponentials or Laplace transforms.&lt;SEP&gt;The homogeneous state equation is a differential equation represented as \dot{x} = Ax, where A is a matrix and x is a vector. It describes the dynamics of a system without external inputs.&lt;SEP&gt;The homogeneous state equation is a form of a linear time-invariant state equation, solved in the text.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e036712f5b53112186f8d26bf732a1a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51b7aad7be1a3e458fc1c221ae0abd4d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c788b304947ce9ba784353e01e43778</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Scalar Differential Equation">
  <data key="d0">Scalar Differential Equation</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The scalar differential equation is a simple form of differential equation used as a basis for solving more complex equations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e036712f5b53112186f8d26bf732a1a5</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Matrix Exponential">
  <data key="d0">Matrix Exponential</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Matrix Exponential is a concept in linear algebra that represents an infinite power series similar to a scalar exponential. It is a mathematical function integral to solving systems of linear differential equations and is widely used in state-space analysis and control engineering problems. The matrix exponential provides solutions in terms of exponential functions of matrices and is represented as \( e^{At} \), where \( A \) is a matrix. This mathematical operation offers a convenient means for finding closed solutions for matrix equations and is crucial for formulating the state-transition matrix. Additionally, the computation of the matrix exponential can involve techniques such as Sylvester’s interpolation formula.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9c788b304947ce9ba784353e01e43778&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-baf80d031591815111410b79dbb30df9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51b7aad7be1a3e458fc1c221ae0abd4d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-020147c9c5bc8be22c285fdcc01a4a4c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-660f747fbdc575c7df68ed347887ea9e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9c2225c69899b581fb582e25a195224</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Power Series">
  <data key="d0">Power Series</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">A series of terms in the form of a polynomial, used to express functions in terms of powers of a variable.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c9c2225c69899b581fb582e25a195224</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="State-Space Analysis">
  <data key="d0">State-Space Analysis</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">A method used in control theory to model and analyze systems using state variables.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c9c2225c69899b581fb582e25a195224</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="State-Transition Matrix">
  <data key="d0">State-Transition Matrix</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">State-Transition Matrix is a matrix used to describe the transitions of a state in a dynamic system, often used in control theory and signal processing.&lt;SEP&gt;State-Transition Matrix is used to describe the transitions of state variables over time in a dynamic system.&lt;SEP&gt;The State-Transition Matrix, denoted as Φ(t), is a mathematical construct used to describe the evolution of a system's state over time.&lt;SEP&gt;The state-transition matrix, denoted as $e^{\mathbf{A}t}$, describes the evolution of a system's state over time.&lt;SEP&gt;The state-transition matrix, denoted as Φ(t), is a mathematical matrix used to describe the free motions of a system. It is a solution to the homogeneous state equation and contains information about the system's dynamics.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9c788b304947ce9ba784353e01e43778&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51b7aad7be1a3e458fc1c221ae0abd4d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76155cfacd298ba99866d06587bc0e7d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf7ceea51cabf1fcb837b2df7b1f884d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d2f61e38a659adbd5279f14d8bc0af8f</data>
