  <data key="d2">Cayley–Hamilton Theorem states that every square matrix satisfies its own characteristic equation.&lt;SEP&gt;The Cayley–Hamilton Theorem states that every square matrix satisfies its own characteristic equation.&lt;SEP&gt;The Cayley–Hamilton theorem is a fundamental theorem in linear algebra stating that every square matrix satisfies its own characteristic equation.&lt;SEP&gt;The Cayley–Hamilton theorem is a principle in linear algebra that states a matrix satisfies its own characteristic equation.</data>
