<node id="Minimal Polynomial">
  <data key="d0">Minimal Polynomial</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The minimal polynomial is a unique, monic polynomial of the smallest degree that annihilates a given matrix, meaning it results in the zero matrix when evaluated at the matrix. It serves an important role in matrix computations, particularly in providing information about the eigenvalues of the matrix and in matrix function calculations. The minimal polynomial is the least-degree polynomial that a matrix satisfies, and in certain cases, it can be identical to the characteristic polynomial of the matrix. This concept is fundamental in matrix theory and is used as an alternative in specific computational situations involving matrices.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ee2367bed52d64be4e9f7ebf2e7d2966&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37b218740e6a890184b54e5af8f87969&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-020147c9c5bc8be22c285fdcc01a4a4c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d534b62ef294c9d4ff9c22bb3b8e45e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c7b0a8292525cb7105c4e499daefad79&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7945bed4da5ce5553ce109cfbcbf173d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ed9a9bbc29b199320adff0a750dad8d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d2f61e38a659adbd5279f14d8bc0af8f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a587ec6eec2d51c833758323b1607ad7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-660f747fbdc575c7df68ed347887ea9e</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
