<node id="Inverse Matrix">
  <data key="d0">Inverse Matrix</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The Inverse Matrix is a mathematical operation applied to matrices that plays a crucial role in solving systems of linear equations. It is defined as a matrix that, when multiplied with the original matrix, results in the identity matrix. This property allows the inverse matrix to reverse the effects of the original matrix. Calculating the inverse matrix is essential for various applications, including determining the state transition matrix, which is vital for solving certain systems, such as those involving (sI - A).</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-650fe4ece98a68e3b77fbb33b8efcab8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c35c8384335c3eddd1b49dc9cad5f9cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3eada2cca3adbe3abcd9f22269177170&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a5b38ba15c11c9500daafd6a0fa68942&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f77aa7cb3bbb0d81fa13d3094e137d99&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-576041b0bc4054622300c536ef926759</data>
