<node id="Matrix Q">
  <data key="d0">Matrix Q</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Matrix Q is a crucial component in the quadratic optimal control problem, where it serves multiple integral roles. Primarily, it is a matrix involved in the performance index calculation and system dynamics, used to weigh the state variables. Matrix Q is often constructed as a diagonal matrix, which influences the weight of state variables in the performance index, thereby determining the importance of errors. It is a positive-definite Hermitian or real symmetric matrix, ensuring the stability and reliability of the system. Matrix Q also plays a role in evaluating the controllability of a system, frequently involving other matrices such as A, B, and C. Additionally, it is engaged in mathematical transformations and equations pertinent to system analysis. Overall, Matrix Q is a versatile and essential element in the formulation and solution of quadratic optimal control problems.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d634460bf0500e11bc074875672732ca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4413c8298743c78468e47ffbe0e228a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef23f0827a35b7fb671dc50cf6d63ea0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7901b85c41f86e4c8c10a0b273e9c765&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d1c6b6475b03e27e6db3ac883a90115c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27adbbe8c3daf01de8b63ffa252de1e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-58531aa8deb3e186c6997e9b42da144f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6daa8560d2825569846748debe43a15</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
