<node id="State Feedback Gain Matrix">
  <data key="d0">State Feedback Gain Matrix</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The State Feedback Gain Matrix, denoted as matrix K, is a mathematical construct used in control systems to determine optimal control signals for adjusting system behavior. It plays a crucial role in the control signal equation, where it adjusts state feedback to achieve desired system dynamics and closed-loop pole placement. By determining feedback gains for state variables, the matrix K helps design controllers that ensure desired system behavior, typically through pole placement, allowing for precise control of system dynamics.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9f818528633d493e4d171630e04e1d9b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e863c1a50016793179faa1e0b91cb9df&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ece149736a8793b07c50dccb1028cee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63ee60925a95b0307b6e89fce826e877&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-31df32fb8d3f0302ba80571341b33840&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f99b64d34db6511197d521a024a4930&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8258faffcaea77860b8003c251cb0674&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-12d9f86a0ab5347bed74adfcf7735e09&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1acc9332423db1bbcc93fc2b0ec7e34d</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Pole-Placement Scheme">
  <data key="d0">Pole-Placement Scheme</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The Pole-Placement Scheme is a method in control systems design that specifies the placement of closed-loop poles to achieve desired system characteristics.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8258faffcaea77860b8003c251cb0674</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Regulator System">
  <data key="d0">Regulator System</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The Regulator System is a type of control system designed to regulate the output of a plant to achieve desired performance metrics such as maximum overshoot and settling time. It aims to maintain zero output despite disturbances, with the reference input always set to zero. This system involves controlling system parameters through feedback mechanisms to ensure optimal performance. It includes components such as an observer controller and is described by a transfer function, which is utilized to analyze control strategies, including pole placement. The Regulator System is responsible for returning the cart to its reference position at the end of each control process, and it encompasses the broader control system, including its components and mathematical models.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f599210548e4a595268cbd4a1d4b5e3c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7abd7647d540dcfe486743c3fa15b49c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a6c1f27816ba00765df34580fd4352b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cff8b4398a7527756d649d91c3b5802&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7bd9d9a9ccff6dcc7aa39644785f5940&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2602a3aebfee4edc08475d0264ce7134&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8258faffcaea77860b8003c251cb0674&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9838df333da6616701c1cce66c00e732</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="State Feedback">
  <data key="d0">State Feedback</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">A control strategy where the controller uses the state of the system to compute the control input.&lt;SEP&gt;State Feedback is a control strategy where the control signal is determined by the current state of the system.&lt;SEP&gt;State feedback refers to a control system strategy where the state variables are used to regulate the system's behavior.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-94456e2884706eeb42e67b6c40918a79&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8258faffcaea77860b8003c251cb0674&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ad1dc64fc9b2da439067495b6c1bf166</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
