<node id="Ackermann's Formula">
  <data key="d0">Ackermann's Formula</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Ackermann's Formula is a mathematical approach used for pole placement in control systems, allowing for the determination of the observer gain matrix.&lt;SEP&gt;Ackermann's Formula is a mathematical method used in control theory for designing control systems, particularly for pole placement.&lt;SEP&gt;Ackermann's Formula is a method used in control theory for pole placement in single-input systems, implemented in MATLAB's 'acker' command.&lt;SEP&gt;Ackermann's Formula is a method used in control theory to compute the gain matrix for state feedback controllers.&lt;SEP&gt;Ackermann's Formula is a method used to obtain the state observer gain matrix in control systems.</data>
