<node id="Type 1 Servo System">
  <data key="d0">Type 1 Servo System</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The Type 1 Servo System is a control system configuration that is characterized by its ability to track step inputs with zero steady-state error. It is often used for precise control applications and is designed to achieve asymptotic stability by placing closed-loop poles at desired positions. This system utilizes state feedback to regulate system output, specifically when the plant lacks an integrator, and includes a state observer for control purposes, making it a popular choice in engineering and control systems. Additionally, the Type 1 Servo System may incorporate an integrator in the feedforward path to effectively manage systems without an integrator, ensuring the transformation of input signals into output signals with specific dynamics.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6f805ff2e429256924500b3bb528e1bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7abd7647d540dcfe486743c3fa15b49c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76155cfacd298ba99866d06587bc0e7d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-45733531e78141284083da760089b754&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-389ed190c89a251c5214072489791123&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-761f357930e8cb4b1f367ec8167a5238&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-87f3dae9453dc00aeaa24b0a25b4f9e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ad73b7beb45180631dd72fbab2b6c9b</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
