<node id="State Observer">
  <data key="d0">State Observer</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">A State Observer is a system used in control theory to estimate the internal state of a system based on its outputs and inputs. It plays a crucial role in control systems by estimating unmeasurable state variables, which is essential for the functioning of a Type 1 servo system. This estimation process ensures complete observability of the system and allows for the generation of optimal control signals. The State Observer is designed to provide accurate assessments of the internal state variables by utilizing measurements from the output and control variables, making it a fundamental component in the effective operation of control systems.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8051d18cbff63321d1754c1c1f43cd85&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e863c1a50016793179faa1e0b91cb9df&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76155cfacd298ba99866d06587bc0e7d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-45733531e78141284083da760089b754&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac56253b9f22aee18032b4cf99f1d27d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-39704bca2c3f08c736c74b4257605c0a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-16d9cf4a88154292d8f7994b72a870f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5c7e0dc112b305ed237d6ecd3031c05</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Inverted-Pendulum Control System">
  <data key="d0">Inverted-Pendulum Control System</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
