<node id="Full-Order State Observer">
  <data key="d0">Full-Order State Observer</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">A full-order state observer estimates all state variables of the system, regardless of their measurability.&lt;SEP&gt;A full-order state observer is a system designed to estimate the internal states of a system based on its outputs and inputs.&lt;SEP&gt;A method used in control systems to estimate the internal state of a system based on its outputs and inputs.&lt;SEP&gt;Full-Order State Observer is a method for state estimation in dynamic systems, using equations to track all state variables and outputs.&lt;SEP&gt;The full-order state observer is a model that corrects the output of a plant by comparing estimated and actual outputs, aiming for error convergence.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ac56253b9f22aee18032b4cf99f1d27d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-39704bca2c3f08c736c74b4257605c0a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2bcf605f83825a20ced09f3cfbb124a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f4f9bb3635034fef2739f071dc807bf7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-040d64011f55ec07f471f024c2b1be29</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Reduced-Order State Observer">
  <data key="d0">Reduced-Order State Observer</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">A reduced-order state observer estimates fewer than the total number of state variables, focusing only on those that are unmeasurable.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ac56253b9f22aee18032b4cf99f1d27d</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Minimum-Order State Observer">
  <data key="d0">Minimum-Order State Observer</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">A minimum-order state observer is a reduced-order observer that estimates the minimum possible number of state variables.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ac56253b9f22aee18032b4cf99f1d27d</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Observer Gain Matrix">
  <data key="d0">Observer Gain Matrix</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The Observer Gain Matrix, often denoted as \( \mathbf{K}_{e} \) or Ke, is a mathematical construct used in control theory, specifically in observer-based control systems. Its primary function is to adjust the estimated state feedback to enhance the performance of state observers. By modifying the eigenvalues, the Observer Gain Matrix helps design state observers with desired characteristics, such as stability and speed of response. It acts as a weighting matrix in the correction term, improving the accuracy of the observer's estimation of the system state to align it more closely with the actual state. Additionally, it adjusts feedback signals to account for disturbances and measurement noises, thereby refining the observer's estimation of the plant's state.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8051d18cbff63321d1754c1c1f43cd85&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf54b3d3fa835e379c76e3ccf4ecfa3f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-12121eebc019284d55e0c84cd019271d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cff8b4398a7527756d649d91c3b5802&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-31df32fb8d3f0302ba80571341b33840&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac56253b9f22aee18032b4cf99f1d27d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6aa727c1ad6dddc07c40ad930aae27a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ebe8a3128b2b3aabe653cb149142a6e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5c7e0dc112b305ed237d6ecd3031c05&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-008977814adc708a3eb952aa138c8696</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Observability Condition">
  <data key="d0">Observability Condition</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The observability condition is a requirement that must be satisfied to design state observers.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ac56253b9f22aee18032b4cf99f1d27d</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Estimation Error">
  <data key="d0">Estimation Error</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Estimation error is the difference between the measured output and the estimated output.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ac56253b9f22aee18032b4cf99f1d27d</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Signal Processing Flowchart">
  <data key="d0">Signal Processing Flowchart</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">A flowchart illustrating the process of signal processing, including input processing, signal processing, and output generation with feedback loop.&lt;SEP&gt;The signal processing flowchart is a diagram that illustrates the stages and operations involved in processing signals from input to output.&lt;SEP&gt;The signal processing flowchart outlines the process of handling input and output signals, divided into two main sections.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7abd7647d540dcfe486743c3fa15b49c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c0dd560e406cc5769efa44c166402303&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2bcf605f83825a20ced09f3cfbb124a8</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
