<node id="Plant Model">
  <data key="d0">Plant Model</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The Plant Model represents the system being controlled, which is adjusted using feedback from the observer gain matrix.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0ae81e09d61ed423567970de31eac0a6</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Observer Poles">
  <data key="d0">Observer Poles</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Observer Poles are specific locations in the complex plane, also referred to as the s-plane, where the poles of an observer in control systems are placed. These poles are chosen values that influence the behavior of the observer, particularly affecting the speed and stability of the observer's error decay. In control system design, placing observer poles at specific locations ensures system stability and desired estimation dynamics. In the context provided, Observer Poles are set to a value of -10, which is a specific choice made to influence the system's performance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8051d18cbff63321d1754c1c1f43cd85&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-681185e57d810ae79c2ee826ac8ba784&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2602a3aebfee4edc08475d0264ce7134&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3372436c8d88f158b8e5ef00d0368411&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5ab66ab2ea102011daec41a066d3877c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e83e0b0f093a4a5ee928c26cb73ad75</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Controller Poles">
  <data key="d0">Controller Poles</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Controller poles are values that influence the system's response speed and stability, usually slower than observer poles.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8051d18cbff63321d1754c1c1f43cd85</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
