<node id="Minimum-Order Observer">
  <data key="d0">Minimum-Order Observer</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The Minimum-Order Observer is a concept in control theory and systems engineering, designed to estimate the state of a system with minimal complexity and reduced computational resources. It functions as a reduced-order observer, specifically tailored to estimate unmeasured state variables while minimizing the number of states required for the estimation process. This system is particularly useful in control systems, where it utilizes fewer sensors than the number of state variables and employs second-order models to achieve its objectives. By focusing on estimating only the unmeasured state variables, the Minimum-Order Observer effectively reduces the computational complexity and resource requirements, while ensuring stability and performance. This approach allows for efficient monitoring and control of the system, represented by the plant, based on its inputs and outputs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-baf80d031591815111410b79dbb30df9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a4e4ced27e2780342dd0d29aa11c621b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5ab66ab2ea102011daec41a066d3877c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae9d94f8cb3004790ff22f37200c200d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f4f9bb3635034fef2739f071dc807bf7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-caeb6d047b3cd8348a555d68841dee56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-670bc9d19f233014556f6058e19da1a2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3372436c8d88f158b8e5ef00d0368411&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1db318b25ae401b0bef5ad1a5d9a160&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-12d9f86a0ab5347bed74adfcf7735e09&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6aa727c1ad6dddc07c40ad930aae27a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c5b8198217ef0317fadb7c0c3009acb</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
