<node id="Matrix R">
  <data key="d0">Matrix R</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Matrix R is a crucial component in the quadratic optimal control problem, serving as a part of the performance index to weigh control inputs. It can be either a scalar or a matrix, specifically a positive-definite Hermitian or real symmetric matrix, which accounts for the energy expenditure of control signals. Its primary function is to influence the weighting of control inputs in the performance index calculation for quadratic optimal regulators, ensuring efficient control input management.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d634460bf0500e11bc074875672732ca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4413c8298743c78468e47ffbe0e228a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7901b85c41f86e4c8c10a0b273e9c765&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d1c6b6475b03e27e6db3ac883a90115c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-58531aa8deb3e186c6997e9b42da144f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6daa8560d2825569846748debe43a15</data>
