  <data key="d2">A control strategy where the input to the system is adjusted based on the state of the system to achieve desired performance.&lt;SEP&gt;A control strategy where the system's state is used to calculate the control input to stabilize the system.&lt;SEP&gt;State-Feedback Control is a method used in control systems to stabilize or control a system by feeding back its state.&lt;SEP&gt;State-feedback control is a method used in control systems to adjust the inputs based on the state of the system.&lt;SEP&gt;State-feedback control is a method used to modify system behavior by adjusting inputs.</data>
