  <data key="d0">Nonlinear Plant</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">A nonlinear plant refers to a system whose model is linearized, resulting in unstructured uncertainty due to differences between the actual and modeled dynamics.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-338b0c8db14460db8abd15b27fa186d5</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Small-Gain Theorem">
  <data key="d0">Small-Gain Theorem</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Small-Gain Theorem is used to determine the condition for robust stability in the closed-loop system.&lt;SEP&gt;The Small-Gain Theorem provides a sufficient condition for the stability of a closed-loop system by ensuring that the H-infinity norm of the product of transfer functions is less than one.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-628acd072f30f988c00d9ed5e372af6c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22fe71b0a3b0bfd6d1c5fc705ff0b202</data>
