<node id="Matrix Differential Equation">
  <data key="d0">Matrix Differential Equation</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The matrix differential equation is used to describe the dynamics of a system, involving a stable matrix A and a positive-definite Hermitian matrix.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd576c10a0963ba5c33eef163a461a22</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Hermitian Matrix">
  <data key="d0">Hermitian Matrix</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">A Hermitian matrix is a complex square matrix that is equal to its own conjugate transpose, used in proving stability in systems.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd576c10a0963ba5c33eef163a461a22</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Stable Matrix">
  <data key="d0">Stable Matrix</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">A stable matrix in this context is one whose eigenvalues have negative real parts, ensuring asymptotic stability of the system.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd576c10a0963ba5c33eef163a461a22</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Positive-Definite Matrix">
  <data key="d0">Positive-Definite Matrix</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">A positive-definite matrix is one where the Hermitian form is positive for all non-zero vectors, crucial for proving stability.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd576c10a0963ba5c33eef163a461a22</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Hermitian Matrix P">
  <data key="d0">Hermitian Matrix P</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Hermitian Matrix P is a positive-definite matrix that satisfies the equation A*P + PA = -Q, ensuring system stability.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd576c10a0963ba5c33eef163a461a22</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Stable Matrix A">
  <data key="d0">Stable Matrix A</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Matrix A is a constant matrix with eigenvalues having negative real parts, ensuring the asymptotic stability of the system.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd576c10a0963ba5c33eef163a461a22</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Positive-Definite Matrix Q">
  <data key="d0">Positive-Definite Matrix Q</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Matrix Q is a positive-definite Hermitian matrix used in conjunction with matrix A to ensure system stability.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd576c10a0963ba5c33eef163a461a22</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
