  <data key="d0">Cauchy–Riemann Conditions</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Cauchy–Riemann Conditions are mathematical conditions used to determine if a function is holomorphic.&lt;SEP&gt;Cauchy–Riemann conditions are mathematical criteria used to determine if a function is analytic.&lt;SEP&gt;The Cauchy–Riemann Conditions are a set of partial differential equations which, when satisfied, indicate that a complex function is analytic.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-284ad82d5a54aa2c3d44aa8399b9ac0c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-faf6d229bd33d9a677ddb2c4f3fe8552&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-989ef45348532327c1757ed1c157833e</data>
