<node id="Determinant">
  <data key="d0">Determinant</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The determinant is a mathematical concept that is essential in various applications involving matrices. It is a scalar value derived from the elements of a square matrix, and it encapsulates and encodes important properties of the matrix. This value plays a crucial role in solving systems of linear equations and is instrumental in determining the invertibility of matrices.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3799700b8e604e5c5384e0643a874e09&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-650fe4ece98a68e3b77fbb33b8efcab8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3eada2cca3adbe3abcd9f22269177170&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa799608fb083db3887d5b7460525b5b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-faf6d229bd33d9a677ddb2c4f3fe8552&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-576041b0bc4054622300c536ef926759</data>
  <data key="d4">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</node>
<node id="Adjoint Matrix">
  <data key="d0">Adjoint Matrix</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Adjoint Matrix is the transpose of the cofactor matrix, used in calculating the inverse of a matrix.&lt;SEP&gt;Adjoint Matrix is the transpose of the matrix of cofactors and is used in various matrix operations.&lt;SEP&gt;The adjoint matrix is used in the computation of the inverse matrix, involving the cofactors of the original matrix.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-650fe4ece98a68e3b77fbb33b8efcab8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa799608fb083db3887d5b7460525b5b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-576041b0bc4054622300c536ef926759</data>
