<edge source="MATLAB" target="Transfer Function">
  <data key="d5">51.0</data>
  <data key="d6">MATLAB is a powerful computational tool widely used in systems and control theory for handling transfer functions. It allows users to transform state-space equations into transfer functions and vice versa, demonstrating its utility in mathematical modeling. MATLAB is employed to analyze, compute, and derive transfer functions of systems, including calculating the transfer function of observer controllers. By using transfer functions, MATLAB provides a basis for modeling and analyzing linear systems, enabling various response analyses.</data>
  <data key="d7">programming, calculation&lt;SEP&gt;software application, mathematical modeling&lt;SEP&gt;software utility, mathematical modeling&lt;SEP&gt;system analysis, computational modeling&lt;SEP&gt;system modeling, linear analysis&lt;SEP&gt;system transformation, mathematical modeling</data>
  <data key="d8">chunk-76155cfacd298ba99866d06587bc0e7d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c59263c3980c23b4b65459cfd0557ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7ee96b6c7a32a3b2a58081228221eda&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-576041b0bc4054622300c536ef926759&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-86ce58db4d75e50b5241f0be0e62c4c5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e75920e90983d6045aaa3f10230d2c07</data>
  <data key="d9">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</edge>
<edge source="MATLAB" target="State-Space Representation">
  <data key="d5">54.0</data>
  <data key="d6">MATLAB is a powerful tool used for modeling and analyzing systems through state-space representation. It facilitates the conversion of transfer functions to state-space forms and vice versa, underscoring its pivotal role in control system analysis and simulation. By providing functions to define systems in state-space form, MATLAB offers a versatile approach that enhances the analysis and simulation capabilities for users working with dynamic systems.</data>
  <data key="d7">numerical computing, transformation&lt;SEP&gt;software application, system modeling&lt;SEP&gt;software utility, system analysis&lt;SEP&gt;system representation, control analysis&lt;SEP&gt;system transformation, numerical computing</data>
  <data key="d8">chunk-76155cfacd298ba99866d06587bc0e7d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c59263c3980c23b4b65459cfd0557ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-04a1c0b94bb767b480f265211df2d3c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-86ce58db4d75e50b5241f0be0e62c4c5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e75920e90983d6045aaa3f10230d2c07&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-180f42dfceafd3c905e78519e41eebca</data>
