  <data key="d5">58.0</data>
  <data key="d6">MATLAB is a versatile software tool that is extensively used to generate Nyquist plots, which are crucial for analyzing the frequency response and stability of control systems. It provides the necessary programming capabilities, toolsets, and functions to create and visualize these plots, aiding engineers and scientists in performing comprehensive system analysis. By utilizing MATLAB, users can effectively conduct system frequency response analysis and assess the stability of control systems through the creation of Nyquist plots.</data>
