<edge source="Bode Diagram" target="Frequency Response">
  <data key="d5">97.0</data>
  <data key="d6">A Bode diagram is a graphical tool used to represent the frequency response of a system, particularly in control systems. It visually illustrates how a system reacts to different frequencies by plotting magnitude and phase angle against frequency. The Bode diagram consists of rectangular plots that provide insights into the system's gain and phase shift variations across a range of frequencies. Through these magnitude and phase plots, the Bode diagram helps analyze and understand the system's behavior in response to varying frequencies.</data>
  <data key="d7">frequency analysis, control system&lt;SEP&gt;graphical representation, control systems&lt;SEP&gt;graphical representation, system analysis&lt;SEP&gt;system analysis, graphical representation&lt;SEP&gt;system analysis, response characterization&lt;SEP&gt;visual representation, system analysis&lt;SEP&gt;visual representation, system behavior&lt;SEP&gt;visualization, system analysis</data>
  <data key="d8">chunk-289220cc5e6fcc41f8da8923ec0e0105&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f0dfc9266a7cbf0daf9292867c654cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a8c47160042a9398aa709e25eded3b0c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-181fee5061e5d9adf0f04d196cc15e7f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b139b34ebbeaf26c5893fedc131b125&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cba4dc46aaf3979ba1619c43d08d1720&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7bfba099219ef0865c8cfbb638e366f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e0c2c5d2084cf4dc42eac20165445910&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d35fea10973c2b24ef34a97da4f0e8b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ccb516dd7fa038fc65484f2cc9669722&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7617e3bbfe2c63a69317713315650eb3</data>
  <data key="d9">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Bode Diagram" target="Transfer Function">
  <data key="d5">67.0</data>
  <data key="d6">The Bode Diagram is a graphical representation used to analyze the frequency response of a system's transfer function. It is derived from the transfer function and provides insights into how the output of a system changes with varying input frequencies. The Bode Diagram simplifies the plotting of frequency-response data, making it easier to analyze system dynamics by visually representing the magnitude and phase characteristics of the transfer function. This tool is crucial for understanding the frequency response characteristics of different transfer functions, offering a clear visualization of their magnitude and phase angle.</data>
  <data key="d7">frequency analysis, system behavior&lt;SEP&gt;frequency response, system analysis&lt;SEP&gt;graphical representation, system analysis&lt;SEP&gt;mathematical modeling, graphical representation&lt;SEP&gt;system analysis, frequency domain&lt;SEP&gt;system analysis, mathematical modeling&lt;SEP&gt;visual representation, frequency response</data>
  <data key="d8">chunk-b2a20c61ffd29ee123aa4008d1f4ba5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-016ebe44f8f410b4e420081ccf7a65f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-289220cc5e6fcc41f8da8923ec0e0105&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4bf77eaf82ba369d832435b0e6f076eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-855fbfd6cc8ae599aa41c969d6418c33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-562db1bae3e6a30605a16f1c339c6e3d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ccb516dd7fa038fc65484f2cc9669722</data>
  <data key="d9">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Bode Diagram" target="Logarithmic Scale">
  <data key="d5">8.0</data>
  <data key="d6">The Logarithmic Scale is employed in Bode diagrams to represent frequency data in a compact form.</data>
  <data key="d7">data representation, frequency analysis</data>
  <data key="d8">chunk-4bf77eaf82ba369d832435b0e6f076eb</data>
  <data key="d9">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Bode Diagram" target="Magnitude Plot">
  <data key="d5">56.0</data>
  <data key="d6">A Bode Diagram is a graphical representation used in engineering and control systems to illustrate the frequency response of a system. It consists of two main components: the Magnitude Plot and the Phase Plot. The Magnitude Plot, specifically, is a crucial component of the Bode Diagram. It displays the system's gain or amplitude response as a function of frequency, effectively detailing how the amplitude varies across different frequencies. The Magnitude Plot provides insight into the system's magnitude response, helping engineers understand how the system amplifies or attenuates signals at various frequencies.</data>
  <data key="d7">amplitude analysis, graphical representation&lt;SEP&gt;diagram component, system gain&lt;SEP&gt;graphical component, frequency analysis&lt;SEP&gt;graphical representation, system gain&lt;SEP&gt;plot component, amplitude analysis&lt;SEP&gt;plot component, frequency analysis&lt;SEP&gt;visual component, frequency analysis</data>
  <data key="d8">chunk-289220cc5e6fcc41f8da8923ec0e0105&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f074d90ecc0d7974d2a0b0c59285149&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-618424e4625f7d33fa3ab142d292d0b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-181fee5061e5d9adf0f04d196cc15e7f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b139b34ebbeaf26c5893fedc131b125&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f6dad58f78a125a7c454b0f2177f13a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ccb516dd7fa038fc65484f2cc9669722</data>
  <data key="d9">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</edge>
