<edge source="Transfer Function" target="Impulse-Response Function">
  <data key="d5">26.0</data>
  <data key="d6">Impulse-response function is related to transfer function in analyzing system behavior.&lt;SEP&gt;The Transfer Function's inverse Laplace Transform yields the Impulse-Response Function, which describes the system's response to a unit-impulse input.&lt;SEP&gt;The impulse-response function and transfer function contain the same information about system dynamics, allowing for analysis through impulse input and measurement of response.</data>
  <data key="d7">system behavior, input-output relationship&lt;SEP&gt;system dynamics, mathematical equivalence&lt;SEP&gt;system response, dynamic characteristics</data>
  <data key="d8">chunk-c4592f010cac7379fc36d89be453d068&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d34b551b0c812125805bc0bfa51cbbdb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c890c6f04ba9977fdf49ac7e887daf46</data>
  <data key="d9">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Transfer Function" target="Laplace Transform">
  <data key="d5">45.0</data>
  <data key="d6">Laplace Transform is used to derive the transfer function from the time-domain representation of a system.&lt;SEP&gt;Laplace transforms are used to derive transfer functions, which describe the input-output relationship of control systems.&lt;SEP&gt;The Laplace Transform is used to derive the Transfer Function by transforming differential equations into algebraic equations.&lt;SEP&gt;The Laplace transform is used to derive the transfer function, facilitating the analysis of the system's dynamics.&lt;SEP&gt;The transfer function is derived using the Laplace transform to relate the input and output in the frequency domain.</data>
  <data key="d7">mathematical modeling, system analysis&lt;SEP&gt;mathematical technique, system analysis&lt;SEP&gt;mathematical transformation, frequency-domain analysis&lt;SEP&gt;mathematical transformation, system analysis</data>
  <data key="d8">chunk-053e8edb648cfc91fffeac7f5faec45b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc700758bd11889bde17fb78bf15e8bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fab839ec7d08f56111abaab896a33188&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c890c6f04ba9977fdf49ac7e887daf46&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-62a1cbf10c33f82d65ca8e2a6d86b67b</data>
  <data key="d9">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Transfer Function" target="Convolution Integral">
  <data key="d5">8.0</data>
  <data key="d6">The Transfer Function relates to the Convolution Integral as the inverse Laplace Transform of the Transfer Function gives the system's impulse response, which is used in the Convolution Integral.</data>
  <data key="d7">system dynamics, mathematical relationship</data>
  <data key="d8">chunk-c890c6f04ba9977fdf49ac7e887daf46</data>
  <data key="d9">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</edge>
