<edge source="Transfer Function" target="Frequency Response">
  <data key="d5">66.0</data>
  <data key="d6">Frequency Response and Transfer Function are closely related concepts in system analysis, particularly in the context of signal processing. The Frequency Response of a system is a critical aspect that describes how the system behaves over a range of input frequencies. This behavior is analyzed through the Transfer Function, which is a mathematical representation that defines the system's frequency response characteristics. The Transfer Function is instrumental in determining the Frequency Response, as it describes how the system's output responds to various input frequencies. This relationship is often depicted in a Nyquist Plot, which visually represents the system's response across different frequencies. Overall, the Transfer Function is essential for deriving and understanding the Frequency Response, providing insights into the system's behavior in response to input signals.</data>
  <data key="d7">mathematical analysis, system behavior&lt;SEP&gt;mathematical modeling, system behavior&lt;SEP&gt;mathematical modeling, system characteristics&lt;SEP&gt;system analysis, mathematical modeling&lt;SEP&gt;system behavior, input-output relationship&lt;SEP&gt;system behavior, mathematical analysis</data>
  <data key="d8">chunk-a104cc76c4ded119be1e066101146986&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98b7da91ec0504b2cb24aec37c61430a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-550487a7cadc4b8eeb83211703d232ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b139b34ebbeaf26c5893fedc131b125&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-484e9407831fd22fae06241d1b7e75e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8a3a4cd5f5a625120a672d9302619e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e0c2c5d2084cf4dc42eac20165445910&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1022a5cf276c07ee56ffc50c13799b6d</data>
  <data key="d9">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</edge>
