</edge>
<edge source="G(s)" target="H(s)">
  <data key="d5">22.0</data>
  <data key="d6">G(s) and H(s) are part of the internal feedback loop, affecting the control system's characteristics at different frequencies.&lt;SEP&gt;G(s) and H(s) are related as parts of a control system's transfer function, often interacting to determine system behavior.&lt;SEP&gt;H(s) provides feedback to G(s) to ensure the control system corrects deviations from the setpoint.</data>
  <data key="d7">feedback loop, system modification&lt;SEP&gt;feedback loop, system regulation&lt;SEP&gt;system components, feedback</data>
  <data key="d8">chunk-e67cb8477adc7c0ef97482e4e7be7fa4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd104ba0a5d1c1ab6f6f3b08f2715be8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76bc75a542f1bbffc63059af2a43bbeb</data>
