<edge source="G1(s)" target="G2(s)">
  <data key="d5">27.0</data>
  <data key="d6">G1(s) and G2(s) are components of the transfer function G(s) affecting the overall system stability.&lt;SEP&gt;G1(s) and G2(s) are interconnected, participating in the modification of signal flow within the system.&lt;SEP&gt;G1(s) and G2(s) are related through their sinusoidal transfer function equations, exhibiting symmetry.&lt;SEP&gt;G2(s) is chosen to stabilize the system by compensating for the instability of G1(s).</data>
  <data key="d7">component interaction, signal modification&lt;SEP&gt;component interaction, transfer function&lt;SEP&gt;equation relationship, symmetry&lt;SEP&gt;system stability, component interaction</data>
