<edge source="R(s)" target="C(s)">
  <data key="d5">35.0</data>
  <data key="d6">C(s) and R(s) are components of the system's transfer function in the Laplace domain, indicating input-output relationships.&lt;SEP&gt;R(s) and C(s) represent the input and output signals in the block diagram, showing the transformation process.&lt;SEP&gt;R(s) is the input signal processed to achieve the desired output C(s) in control systems.&lt;SEP&gt;R(s) serves as the input to the control system, and C(s) is the resulting output after processing through the gain element K.</data>
  <data key="d7">input-output relation, control system&lt;SEP&gt;input-output relationship, signal processing&lt;SEP&gt;input-output relationship, signal transformation&lt;SEP&gt;signal representation, transfer function</data>
