  <data key="d5">14.0</data>
  <data key="d6">R(s) and E(s) are components of a control system where E(s) is derived from the difference between R(s) and the actual output.&lt;SEP&gt;R(s) provides the input signal that is compared by E(s) to detect errors in the control system.</data>
