<edge source="Feedback Loop" target="Control System">
  <data key="d5">46.0</data>
  <data key="d6">Feedback loops are integral components of control systems, used to stabilize and manage system behavior.&lt;SEP&gt;The control system utilizes a feedback loop to regulate and adjust its output based on the difference between the desired and actual performance.&lt;SEP&gt;The feedback loop is a critical component of the control system, enabling continuous performance monitoring and adjustment.&lt;SEP&gt;The feedback loop is a mechanism within the control system to regulate its behavior.&lt;SEP&gt;The feedback loop is essential for the control system to adjust its behavior based on the output.</data>
  <data key="d7">closed-loop control, system regulation&lt;SEP&gt;system management, stability&lt;SEP&gt;system regulation, feedback mechanism&lt;SEP&gt;system regulation, performance adjustment&lt;SEP&gt;system structure, continuous control</data>
  <data key="d8">chunk-cd437ba37843beb72e13fcc99049d49c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7fae43bfb1918de812ae799078e161e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a12a1fcc8b96ef105600adda81cf5b8f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ccfe5606d87942d95cd99b0924a1abcd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03cc52015d502a70a9646315437485f3</data>
  <data key="d9">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</edge>
