<edge source="Matrix A" target="Minimal Polynomial">
  <data key="d5">40.0</data>
  <data key="d6">Matrix A's minimal polynomial is crucial for calculating functions of the matrix using Sylvester's interpolation formula.&lt;SEP&gt;Matrix A's minimal polynomial is identical to its characteristic polynomial due to linked eigenvalues in a Jordan chain.&lt;SEP&gt;Matrix A's minimal polynomial is used in Sylvester’s interpolation formula for computing matrix exponentials.&lt;SEP&gt;The Minimal Polynomial is the least-degree polynomial that Matrix A satisfies, crucial for matrix computations.&lt;SEP&gt;The minimal polynomial is derived from matrix A and provides information about its eigenvalues.</data>
