<edge source="Damping Ratio" target="Closed-Loop Poles">
  <data key="d5">81.0</data>
  <data key="d6">Closed-Loop Poles and Damping Ratio are interconnected entities that play a crucial role in determining system stability and behavior. The Damping Ratio is a characteristic derived from the Closed-Loop Poles, influencing how oscillations decay and affecting the location and behavior of these poles. This relationship is essential for understanding system stability and performance. The Damping Ratio impacts the position of the Closed-Loop Poles, which in turn influences the overall stability and oscillation behavior of the system. By calculating the Damping Ratio from the Closed-Loop Poles, one can assess and predict system behavior, ensuring optimal performance and stability.</data>
