<edge source="Unit-Step Response" target="Compensated System">
  <data key="d5">49.0</data>
  <data key="d6">The Compensated System is evaluated through its Unit-Step Response, which serves as a key indicator of its transient behavior and overall performance. The system demonstrates a more stable unit-step response, characterized by reduced overshoot and faster settling time compared to the uncompensated system. Despite the initial rapid response, where it quickly reaches maximum output, the compensated system ultimately shows improved performance, suggesting a balance between speed and stability. This enhanced response is particularly notable when contrasted with the uncompensated system, which typically exhibits larger maximum overshoot and slower response times. The unit-step response graph effectively illustrates how the compensated system reacts to a unit step input, highlighting its optimized performance metrics.</data>
  <data key="d7">performance analysis, stability assessment&lt;SEP&gt;performance evaluation, response speed&lt;SEP&gt;performance improvement, control engineering&lt;SEP&gt;system behavior, input response&lt;SEP&gt;system dynamics, step input&lt;SEP&gt;system evaluation, performance analysis</data>
  <data key="d8">chunk-896487ddef7a3f411006102c6c7a9b2b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0948b1e428ea01364b1b1ec1955431f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ed1ff4c236c16a58ee408da4a88effc4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a2ddda49062cacf815e40ae9bc8167c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec1fe4f707d8920dbeac015fecfd158e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c3a55af272f2092fd9d053a8d89af4b4</data>
  <data key="d9">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Unit-Step Response" target="Uncompensated System">
  <data key="d5">28.0</data>
  <data key="d6">The Uncompensated System exhibits higher overshoot and slower settling time in its Unit-Step Response.&lt;SEP&gt;The Uncompensated System's unit-step response is faster with less overshoot, contrasting with the compensated system.&lt;SEP&gt;The uncompensated system displays a slower initial response in the unit-step test, taking longer to reach maximum output.&lt;SEP&gt;The uncompensated system's unit-step response serves as a baseline for comparing improvements in the compensated system.</data>
  <data key="d7">baseline comparison, system analysis&lt;SEP&gt;performance evaluation, response speed&lt;SEP&gt;performance limitations, stability issues&lt;SEP&gt;system dynamics, step input</data>
  <data key="d8">chunk-ec1fe4f707d8920dbeac015fecfd158e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-896487ddef7a3f411006102c6c7a9b2b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0948b1e428ea01364b1b1ec1955431f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c3a55af272f2092fd9d053a8d89af4b4</data>
