  <data key="d6">Proportional control alone results in an offset, a type of steady-state error.&lt;SEP&gt;Proportional control systems without integrating properties often experience offset because they cannot eliminate steady-state errors.</data>
  <data key="d7">control limitation, error presence&lt;SEP&gt;control system limitations, steady-state error</data>
  <data key="d8">chunk-cd566e31ec5118dde48a4f149d4c5469&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-39fb7e7ecf98024e40979eb23f0ae0a1</data>
  <data key="d9">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Proportional Control" target="Derivative Control">
  <data key="d5">8.0</data>
  <data key="d6">Proportional control is often combined with derivative control to enhance system stability and response by adding damping.</data>
