<edge source="Compensated System" target="Uncompensated System">
  <data key="d5">72.0</data>
  <data key="d6">The Compensated System is a modified version of the Uncompensated System, designed for improved performance and stability. When compared in terms of unit-step and unit-ramp responses, the Compensated System consistently demonstrates superior performance, outputting higher values than the Uncompensated System. This indicates enhanced performance metrics, including lower steady-state error and improved stability. The Uncompensated System serves as a baseline for comparison, highlighting the advancements made in the Compensated System through various enhancements. Overall, the Compensated System showcases significant improvements in both performance and stability over the Uncompensated System.</data>
