<edge source="Gain Margin" target="Phase Margin">
  <data key="d5">66.0</data>
  <data key="d6">Gain Margin and Phase Margin are both essential metrics used to assess system stability in control systems. These measures are derived from the frequency response analysis, specifically from the Bode Diagram and the G(jω) locus, which are part of the frequency domain analysis. Both Gain Margin and Phase Margin indicate how close a system is to instability, providing crucial insights into the system's performance under various conditions. They are key to understanding and evaluating the stability of a control system, ensuring that it operates reliably and effectively.</data>
  <data key="d7">stability measures, control system design&lt;SEP&gt;stability measures, system robustness&lt;SEP&gt;system stability, control analysis&lt;SEP&gt;system stability, control metrics&lt;SEP&gt;system stability, frequency domain&lt;SEP&gt;system stability, performance metrics</data>
  <data key="d8">chunk-4e42383167231f90ca804ba822f6b73d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-016ebe44f8f410b4e420081ccf7a65f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-289220cc5e6fcc41f8da8923ec0e0105&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-189305ffdfb5a3f7a9695e56559bcef3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-87b0e0bfbf5774f7c90a99f131e0bb53&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e0c2c5d2084cf4dc42eac20165445910&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-731aadaa135cc2ef1c9482aab829f4e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50c4cfa192898028842df51ccba67794</data>
  <data key="d9">Markdown_nofigure.md</data>
</edge>
